<div id="S2.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Applying <math id="S2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{d+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{d+1}</annotation></semantics></math> amounts to choosing a vertex in <math id="S2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{d+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{d+1}</annotation></semantics></math> and fixing its spin to be <math id="S2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. Identifying <math id="S2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(K_{d+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(K_{d+1})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[d+1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[d+1]</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
