</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p12.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemma is a key statement that allows us to use the theory of Lorentzian polynomials.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2.7</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> be an entrywise-positive antiferromagnetic model. For <math id="S2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the clique partition function <math id="S2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is Lorentzian. Consequently, <math id="S2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{d}^{1/d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{d}^{1/d}</annotation></semantics></math> is concave on the positive orthant.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> be the spin set of <math id="S2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>. We prove that <math id="S2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lorentzian by induction on <math id="S2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>; the final assertion then follows from <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Proposition 2.4. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>.
Clearly, <math id="S2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is homogeneous of degree <math id="S2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S2.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is entrywise positive, the support of <math id="S2.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the full degree-<math id="S2.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> simplex <math id="S2.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{{\bm{\alpha}}\in(\mathbb{N}_{0})^{I}:\sum_{\sigma\in I}\alpha_{\sigma}=d\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{\bm{\alpha}}\in(\mathbb{N}_{0})^{I}:\sum_{\sigma\in I}\alpha_{\sigma}=d\}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is readily seen to be M-convex.
When <math id="S2.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1</annotation></semantics></math>, homogeneity and the M-convexity of the support show that <math id="S2.p13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lorentzian; when <math id="S2.p13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p13.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}Z_{d}=2H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}Z_{d}=2H</annotation></semantics></math> is antiferromagnetic, so <math id="S2.p13.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lorentzian.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now assume <math id="S2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix <math id="S2.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in I</annotation></semantics></math>.
By (<a href="#S2.E1" title="Equation 2.1 ‣ Lemma 2.6. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>) with <math id="S2.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="S2.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d-1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{\tau}Z_{d}(\mathbf{x})=dZ_{d-1}(\mathbf{m}_{\tau}\odot\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>τ</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{\tau}Z_{d}(\mathbf{x})=dZ_{d-1}(\mathbf{m}_{\tau}\odot\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="S2.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lorentzian by the inductive hypothesis and <math id="S2.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> is entrywise positive, <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem5" title="Proposition 2.5. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a> shows that <math id="S2.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{\tau}Z_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>τ</mi></msub><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{\tau}Z_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lorentzian. Since this holds for every <math id="S2.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in I</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lorentzian.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p15.1" class="ltx_p">A stronger version without the entrywise positivity hypothesis was proved in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>, Theorem 3.1]</cite> using an extra lemma to show M-convexity in full generality.
For the present paper, <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma 2.7. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.7</span></a> suffices because, in <a href="#S5" title="5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we will reduce the proof of <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 1.2. ‣ 1.1 A vertex-inhomogeneous strengthening ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a> to the entrywise-positive case.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout this and subsequent sections, all random variables take values in finite sets. All logarithms are natural, and we use the convention <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\log 0=0\log(0/0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\log 0=0\log(0/0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. By a <em id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">law</em>, we mean a probability measure on a finite set.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite nonempty set. Let <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=(X_{1},\dots,X_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=(X_{1},\dots,X_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> be an <math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>-valued random vector. For <math id="S3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\subseteq[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\subseteq[m]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in J</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S3.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X_{J}\coloneqq(X_{i}:i\in J)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{J}\coloneqq(X_{i}:i\in J)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{J\setminus j}\coloneqq X_{J\setminus\{j\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{J\setminus j}\coloneqq X_{J\setminus\{j\}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Given a law <math id="S3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and a random vector <math id="S3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{1},\dots,X_{m})\sim\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{1},\dots,X_{m})\sim\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, write <math id="S3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i}\coloneqq\mathcal{L}(X_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i}\coloneqq\mathcal{L}(X_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> for the <math id="S3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th marginal of <math id="S3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We first recall standard entropy identities and variational formulae; for more background, see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>. In <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, we apply them to exchangeable Lorentzian laws to derive our entropy inequalities.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Entropy and relative entropy</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> be a law on <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>. The <em id="S3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">entropy</em> of <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Ent(\mu)\coloneqq-\sum_{\omega\in\Omega}\mu(\omega)\log\mu(\omega)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≔</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></munder><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ent(\mu)\coloneqq-\sum_{\omega\in\Omega}\mu(\omega)\log\mu(\omega).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We use the elementary fact that entropy is concave: if <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{1},\ldots,\nu_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{1},\ldots,\nu_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are laws on <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1},\ldots,p_{n}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1},\ldots,p_{n}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}p_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}p_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Ent\biggl(\,\sum_{i=1}^{n}p_{i}\nu_{i}\biggr)\geq\sum_{i=1}^{n}p_{i}\Ent(\nu_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ent\biggl(\,\sum_{i=1}^{n}p_{i}\nu_{i}\biggr)\geq\sum_{i=1}^{n}p_{i}\Ent(\nu_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">This follows from concavity of the function <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\mapsto-t\log t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\mapsto-t\log t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> be random variables. The entropy <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Ent(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ent(X)</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Ent(\mathcal{L}(X))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ent(\mathcal{L}(X))</annotation></semantics></math>. Let</p>
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Ent(X\mid Y)\coloneqq\sum_{y:\Pr(Y=y)&gt;0}\Pr(Y=y)\Ent(X\mid Y=y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ent(X\mid Y)\coloneqq\sum_{y:\Pr(Y=y)&gt;0}\Pr(Y=y)\Ent(X\mid Y=y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Ent(X\mid Y=y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ent(X\mid Y=y)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the entropy of the conditional law <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(X\mid Y=y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(X\mid Y=y)</annotation></semantics></math>. Equivalently, <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Ent(X\mid Y)=\Ent(X,Y)-\Ent(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ent(X\mid Y)=\Ent(X,Y)-\Ent(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Ent(X,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ent(X,Y)</annotation></semantics></math> is the entropy of the joint law of <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>.
The <em id="S3.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">mutual information</em> between <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mI(X;Y)\coloneqq\Ent(X)+\Ent(Y)-\Ent(X,Y)=\Ent(X)-\Ent(X\mid Y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mI(X;Y)\coloneqq\Ent(X)+\Ent(Y)-\Ent(X,Y)=\Ent(X)-\Ent(X\mid Y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> be laws on <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\ll\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\ll\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(\omega)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\omega)=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\in\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\in\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu(\omega)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu(\omega)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. The <em id="S3.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">relative entropy</em> <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)\coloneqq\sum_{\omega\in\Omega}\mu(\omega)\log\frac{\mu(\omega)}{\nu(\omega)}=\sup_{f\colon\Omega\to\mathbb{R}}\bigl\{\Ex_{\mu}f-\log\Ex_{\nu}e^{f}\bigr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>f</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)\coloneqq\sum_{\omega\in\Omega}\mu(\omega)\log\frac{\mu(\omega)}{\nu(\omega)}=\sup_{f\colon\Omega\to\mathbb{R}}\bigl\{\Ex_{\mu}f-\log\Ex_{\nu}e^{f}\bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The supremum representation is the <em id="S3.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">variational formula for relative entropy</em>, also known as the Donsker–Varadhan variational formula; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, Appendix C.2]</cite>. Relative entropy is nonnegative, with equality if and only if <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\nu</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\not\ll\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>≪̸</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\not\ll\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, we use the convention <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)=+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)=+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Chain rule for relative entropy)<span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> be laws on <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Xi</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite set and let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\colon\Omega\to\Xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\colon\Omega\to\Xi</annotation></semantics></math> be a map. Assume <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\ll\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\ll\nu</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ν</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be the pushforward laws on <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Xi</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\prime}(\xi)\coloneqq\Pr_{X\sim\mu}(T(X)=\xi),\qquad\nu^{\prime}(\xi)\coloneqq\Pr_{X\sim\nu}(T(X)=\xi)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ν</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\prime}(\xi)\coloneqq\Pr_{X\sim\mu}(T(X)=\xi),\qquad\nu^{\prime}(\xi)\coloneqq\Pr_{X\sim\nu}(T(X)=\xi).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)=D(\mu^{\prime}\mathbin{\|}\nu^{\prime})+\Ex_{Y\sim\mu^{\prime}}D(\mu(\makebox[4.30554pt]{$\cdot$}\!\mid T=Y)\mathbin{\|}\nu(\makebox[4.30554pt]{$\cdot$}\!\mid T=Y))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:4.3pt;" width="4.3pt"><mo>⋅</mo></mpadded><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:4.3pt;" width="4.3pt"><mo>⋅</mo></mpadded><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)=D(\mu^{\prime}\mathbin{\|}\nu^{\prime})+\Ex_{Y\sim\mu^{\prime}}D(\mu(\makebox[4.30554pt]{$\cdot$}\!\mid T=Y)\mathbin{\|}\nu(\makebox[4.30554pt]{$\cdot$}\!\mid T=Y)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Xi_{+}\coloneqq\{\xi\in\Xi:\mu^{\prime}(\xi)&gt;0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Xi_{+}\coloneqq\{\xi\in\Xi:\mu^{\prime}(\xi)&gt;0\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We then rewrite <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)=\sum_{\xi\in\Xi_{+}}\sum_{\omega\in T^{-1}(\xi)}\mu(\omega)\log\frac{\mu(\omega)}{\nu(\omega)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)=\sum_{\xi\in\Xi_{+}}\sum_{\omega\in T^{-1}(\xi)}\mu(\omega)\log\frac{\mu(\omega)}{\nu(\omega)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">As <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\ll\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\ll\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu^{\prime}(\xi)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ν</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu^{\prime}(\xi)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> holds for every <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\in\Xi_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\in\Xi_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, for <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\in\Xi_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\in\Xi_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\in T^{-1}(\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\in T^{-1}(\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(\omega)=\mu^{\prime}(\xi)\mu(\omega\mid T=\xi),\qquad\nu(\omega)=\nu^{\prime}(\xi)\nu(\omega\mid T=\xi)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ν</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\omega)=\mu^{\prime}(\xi)\mu(\omega\mid T=\xi),\qquad\nu(\omega)=\nu^{\prime}(\xi)\nu(\omega\mid T=\xi).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting these into (<a href="#S3.E2" title="Equation 3.2 ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.1 Entropy and relative entropy ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\xi\in\Xi_{+}}\sum_{\omega\in T^{-1}(\xi)}\mu(\omega)\log\frac{\mu^{\prime}(\xi)}{\nu^{\prime}(\xi)}+\sum_{\xi\in\Xi_{+}}\sum_{\omega\in T^{-1}(\xi)}\mu(\omega)\log\frac{\mu(\omega\mid T=\xi)}{\nu(\omega\mid T=\xi)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ν</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\xi\in\Xi_{+}}\sum_{\omega\in T^{-1}(\xi)}\mu(\omega)\log\frac{\mu^{\prime}(\xi)}{\nu^{\prime}(\xi)}+\sum_{\xi\in\Xi_{+}}\sum_{\omega\in T^{-1}(\xi)}\mu(\omega)\log\frac{\mu(\omega\mid T=\xi)}{\nu(\omega\mid T=\xi)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=D(\mu^{\prime}\mathbin{\|}\nu^{\prime})+\sum_{\xi\in\Xi_{+}}\mu^{\prime}(\xi)D(\mu(\makebox[4.30554pt]{$\cdot$}\!\mid T=\xi)\mathbin{\|}\nu(\makebox[4.30554pt]{$\cdot$}\!\mid T=\xi)).\qed" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:4.3pt;" width="4.3pt"><mo>⋅</mo></mpadded><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:4.3pt;" width="4.3pt"><mo>⋅</mo></mpadded><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D(\mu^{\prime}\mathbin{\|}\nu^{\prime})+\sum_{\xi\in\Xi_{+}}\mu^{\prime}(\xi)D(\mu(\makebox[4.30554pt]{$\cdot$}\!\mid T=\xi)\mathbin{\|}\nu(\makebox[4.30554pt]{$\cdot$}\!\mid T=\xi)).\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3.2</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Mutual information as relative entropy)<span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For random variables <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mI(X;Y)=\Ex_{Y}[D(\mathcal{L}(X\mid Y)\mathbin{\|}\mathcal{L}(X))]=\sum_{y:\Pr(Y=y)&gt;0}\Pr(Y=y)D(\mathcal{L}(X\mid Y=y)\mathbin{\|}\mathcal{L}(X))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mI(X;Y)=\Ex_{Y}[D(\mathcal{L}(X\mid Y)\mathbin{\|}\mathcal{L}(X))]=\sum_{y:\Pr(Y=y)&gt;0}\Pr(Y=y)D(\mathcal{L}(X\mid Y=y)\mathbin{\|}\mathcal{L}(X)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\coloneqq\mathcal{L}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\coloneqq\mathcal{L}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>, and for each <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(Y=y)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(Y=y)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{y}\coloneqq\mathcal{L}(X\mid Y=y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{y}\coloneqq\mathcal{L}(X\mid Y=y)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu(x)=\sum_{y:\Pr(Y=y)&gt;0}\Pr(Y=y)\mu_{y}(x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(x)=\sum_{y:\Pr(Y=y)&gt;0}\Pr(Y=y)\mu_{y}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">we have <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{y}\ll\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≪</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{y}\ll\mu</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(Y=y)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(Y=y)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mI(X;Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mI(X;Y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Ent(X)-\Ent(X\mid Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Ent(X)-\Ent(X\mid Y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{x}\mu(x)\log\mu(x)+\sum_{y:\Pr(Y=y)&gt;0}\Pr(Y=y)\sum_{x}\mu_{y}(x)\log\mu_{y}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>x</mi></munder></mstyle><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>x</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{x}\mu(x)\log\mu(x)+\sum_{y:\Pr(Y=y)&gt;0}\Pr(Y=y)\sum_{x}\mu_{y}(x)\log\mu_{y}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{y:\Pr(Y=y)&gt;0}\Pr(Y=y)\biggl(\sum_{x}\mu_{y}(x)\log\mu_{y}(x)-\sum_{x}\mu_{y}(x)\log\mu(x)\biggr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>x</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>x</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{y:\Pr(Y=y)&gt;0}\Pr(Y=y)\biggl(\sum_{x}\mu_{y}(x)\log\mu_{y}(x)-\sum_{x}\mu_{y}(x)\log\mu(x)\biggr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{y:\Pr(Y=y)&gt;0}\Pr(Y=y)D(\mu_{y}\mathbin{\|}\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{y:\Pr(Y=y)&gt;0}\Pr(Y=y)D(\mu_{y}\mathbin{\|}\mu)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Ex_{Y}[D(\mathcal{L}(X\mid Y)\mathbin{\|}\mathcal{L}(X))].\qed" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Ex_{Y}[D(\mathcal{L}(X\mid Y)\mathbin{\|}\mathcal{L}(X))].\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The <em id="S3.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Gibbs law</em> associated with <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\colon\Omega\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\colon\Omega\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is the law <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{f}(\omega)\coloneqq e^{f(\omega)}/Z_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{f}(\omega)\coloneqq e^{f(\omega)}/Z_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{f}\coloneqq\sum_{\omega\in\Omega}e^{f(\omega)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{f}\coloneqq\sum_{\omega\in\Omega}e^{f(\omega)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining this with the variational formula (<a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 3.1 ‣ 3.1 Entropy and relative entropy ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>) for relative entropy gives the <em id="S3.SS1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Gibbs variational formula</em>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3.3</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Gibbs variational formula)<span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\colon\Omega\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\colon\Omega\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log\sum_{\omega\in\Omega}e^{f(\omega)}=\sup_{\mu}\{\Ex_{\mu}f+\Ent(\mu)\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mi>μ</mi></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\sum_{\omega\in\Omega}e^{f(\omega)}=\sup_{\mu}\{\Ex_{\mu}f+\Ent(\mu)\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the supremum is over all laws on <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>. The unique optimizer is the Gibbs law <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> be a law on <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\mu_{f}(\omega)=f(\omega)-\log Z_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\mu_{f}(\omega)=f(\omega)-\log Z_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\mu_{f})=\sum_{\omega\in\Omega}\mu(\omega)\log\frac{\mu(\omega)}{\mu_{f}(\omega)}=\sum_{\omega\in\Omega}\mu(\omega)\log\mu(\omega)-\sum_{\omega\in\Omega}\mu(\omega)\log\mu_{f}(\omega)=-\Ent(\mu)-\Ex_{\mu}f+\log Z_{f}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\mu_{f})=\sum_{\omega\in\Omega}\mu(\omega)\log\frac{\mu(\omega)}{\mu_{f}(\omega)}=\sum_{\omega\in\Omega}\mu(\omega)\log\mu(\omega)-\sum_{\omega\in\Omega}\mu(\omega)\log\mu_{f}(\omega)=-\Ent(\mu)-\Ex_{\mu}f+\log Z_{f}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\mu_{f})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\mu_{f})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, rearranging gives <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Ex_{\mu}f+\Ent(\mu)\leq\log Z_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ex_{\mu}f+\Ent(\mu)\leq\log Z_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>, with equality if and only if <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\mu_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\mu_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking the supremum proves the formula and the uniqueness of the optimizer.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we introduce Lorentzian laws and establish properties that yield a strengthening of a special case of Shearer’s inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, Equation (22)]</cite>; see also <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, Proposition 15.7.4]</cite>. As mentioned in <a href="#S1.SS3" title="1.3 Methodology ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.3</span></a>, Lorentzian laws provide a multiset analogue of the Lorentzian probability measures introduced in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, Section 4.5]</cite>. This is achieved by allowing letters to occur with multiplicity in each word <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\omega}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝎</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\omega}}</annotation></semantics></math> in the sample space. The Lorentzian property of their count-generating polynomials, which will be defined below, allows us to prove a relative entropy contraction (<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 3.5. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>). This yields the desired entropy inequality in <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma 3.7. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Fix a finite set of letters <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\omega}}\in A^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\omega}}\in A^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in A</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{a}({\bm{\omega}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{a}({\bm{\omega}})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the frequency of the letter <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\omega}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝎</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\omega}}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{a}({\bm{\omega}})\coloneqq\lvert\{j\in[m]:\omega_{j}=a\}\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{a}({\bm{\omega}})\coloneqq\lvert\{j\in[m]:\omega_{j}=a\}\rvert</annotation></semantics></math>. Let</p>
<table id="S3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T({\bm{\omega}})\coloneqq(N_{a}({\bm{\omega}}):a\in A)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T({\bm{\omega}})\coloneqq(N_{a}({\bm{\omega}}):a\in A)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">be the <em id="S3.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">count vector</em> of <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\omega}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝎</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\omega}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which counts frequencies of letters in <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\omega}}\in A^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\omega}}\in A^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, all the frequencies sum to <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>. That is, <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T({\bm{\omega}})\in\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T({\bm{\omega}})\in\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A)\coloneqq\{\mathbf{n}\in(\mathbb{N}_{0})^{A}:\sum_{a\in A}n_{a}=m\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A)\coloneqq\{\mathbf{n}\in(\mathbb{N}_{0})^{A}:\sum_{a\in A}n_{a}=m\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a law <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, define its <em id="S3.SS2.p2.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">count law</em> on <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A)</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="S3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})\coloneqq\Pr_{X\sim\mu}(T(X)=\mathbf{n}),\qquad\mathbf{n}\in\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})\coloneqq\Pr_{X\sim\mu}(T(X)=\mathbf{n}),\qquad\mathbf{n}\in\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>A</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the multivariate probability generating function of <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="S3.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mu}(\mathbf{x})\coloneqq\Ex_{Z\sim\pi_{\mu}}\mathbf{x}^{Z}=\Ex_{X\sim\mu}\mathbf{x}^{T(X)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>Z</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mu}(\mathbf{x})\coloneqq\Ex_{Z\sim\pi_{\mu}}\mathbf{x}^{Z}=\Ex_{X\sim\mu}\mathbf{x}^{T(X)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(X)\in\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(X)\in\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>, this is a homogeneous polynomial of degree <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, which we call the <em id="S3.SS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">count-generating polynomial</em> of <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.
We say that <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="S3.SS2.p2.4.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Lorentzian</em> if <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lorentzian.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">A subset <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{m}\subseteq A^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{m}\subseteq A^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is called <em id="S3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">permutation-invariant</em> if it is invariant under permutations of the coordinate positions, i.e., <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\omega_{\pi(1)},\dots,\omega_{\pi(m)})\in\Omega_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\omega_{\pi(1)},\dots,\omega_{\pi(m)})\in\Omega_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> for every permutation <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[m]</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Omega_{\bullet}=(\Omega_{m}:m\geq 1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∙</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{\bullet}=(\Omega_{m}:m\geq 1)</annotation></semantics></math> be a support family. We say that <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{\bullet}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∙</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{\bullet}</annotation></semantics></math> is permutation-invariant if <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is permutation-invariant for all <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, and <em id="S3.SS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">deletion-compatible</em> if, for each <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}\implies{\bm{\omega}}_{[m]\setminus j}\in\Omega_{m-1}\qquad\forall j\in[m]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mi>𝝎</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}\implies{\bm{\omega}}_{[m]\setminus j}\in\Omega_{m-1}\qquad\forall j\in[m].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">A law on <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="S3.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exchangeable</em> if it is invariant under permutations of the coordinate positions.
Let <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{m}(\Omega_{\bullet})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∙</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{m}(\Omega_{\bullet})</annotation></semantics></math> be the family of exchangeable Lorentzian laws supported on <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the remainder of this section, we fix a support family <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{\bullet}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∙</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{\bullet}</annotation></semantics></math> which is permutation-invariant and deletion-compatible, and simply write <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{m}\coloneqq\mathcal{N}_{m}(\Omega_{\bullet})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∙</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{m}\coloneqq\mathcal{N}_{m}(\Omega_{\bullet})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. We identify a law on <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> with the law on <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> obtained by assigning mass zero to <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{m}\setminus\Omega_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{m}\setminus\Omega_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Using the closure properties of Lorentzian polynomials in <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem5" title="Proposition 2.5. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>, we obtain the following properties of exchangeable Lorentzian laws.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.4</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{N}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{N}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\mu</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">the marginal law of </span><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{[m]\setminus j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{[m]\setminus j}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> belongs to </span><math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for each </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in A</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, if </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(X_{j}=a)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(X_{j}=a)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the conditional law </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(X_{[m]\setminus j}\mid X_{j}=a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(X_{[m]\setminus j}\mid X_{j}=a)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> belongs to </span><math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">By exchangeability of <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, it suffices to prove the statement for <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=m</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of <a href="#S3.I1.i1" title="Item (1) ‣ Lemma 3.4. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(1)</span></a>.</span> Let <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu\coloneqq\mathcal{L}(X_{[m-1]})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu\coloneqq\mathcal{L}(X_{[m-1]})</annotation></semantics></math>, which is exchangeable on <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is exchangeable. For <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in A</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{a}\in(\mathbb{N}_{0})^{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{a}\in(\mathbb{N}_{0})^{A}</annotation></semantics></math> be the standard basis vector whose <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>-coordinate is <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. If the event <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{X_{m}=a\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{m}=a\}</annotation></semantics></math> occurs, the count vector of <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{[m-1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{[m-1]}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(X)-\mathbf{e}_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(X)-\mathbf{e}_{a}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, exchangeability of <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> implies that, for <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{n}\in\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{n}\in\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the probability that <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{m}=a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{m}=a</annotation></semantics></math> conditioned on <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(X)=\mathbf{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(X)=\mathbf{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is proportional to the number of occurrences of <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐧</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr_{X\sim\mu}(X_{m}=a\mid T(X)=\mathbf{n})=\frac{n_{a}}{m}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr_{X\sim\mu}(X_{m}=a\mid T(X)=\mathbf{n})=\frac{n_{a}}{m}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, for <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m18" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{x}=(x_{a}:a\in A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}=(x_{a}:a\in A)</annotation></semantics></math>, the count-generating polynomial of <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{\nu}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{\nu}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Ex_{Z\sim\pi_{\nu}}\mathbf{x}^{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>Z</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Ex_{Z\sim\pi_{\nu}}\mathbf{x}^{Z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\mathbf{n}\in\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A):\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})&gt;0}\biggl(\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})\sum_{a\in A:n_{a}&gt;0}\Pr_{X\sim\mu}(X_{m}=a\mid T(X)=\mathbf{n})\,\mathbf{x}^{\mathbf{n}-\mathbf{e}_{a}}\biggr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\mathbf{n}\in\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A):\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})&gt;0}\biggl(\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})\sum_{a\in A:n_{a}&gt;0}\Pr_{X\sim\mu}(X_{m}=a\mid T(X)=\mathbf{n})\,\mathbf{x}^{\mathbf{n}-\mathbf{e}_{a}}\biggr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\mathbf{n}\in\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A):\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})&gt;0}\biggl(\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})\sum_{a\in A:n_{a}&gt;0}\frac{n_{a}}{m}\mathbf{x}^{\mathbf{n}-\mathbf{e}_{a}}\biggr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\mathbf{n}\in\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A):\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})&gt;0}\biggl(\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})\sum_{a\in A:n_{a}&gt;0}\frac{n_{a}}{m}\mathbf{x}^{\mathbf{n}-\mathbf{e}_{a}}\biggr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{a}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{a}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{a}\mathbf{x}^{\mathbf{n}-\mathbf{e}_{a}}=\partial_{a}\mathbf{x}^{\mathbf{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{a}\mathbf{x}^{\mathbf{n}-\mathbf{e}_{a}}=\partial_{a}\mathbf{x}^{\mathbf{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>; otherwise, <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{a}\mathbf{x}^{\mathbf{n}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{a}\mathbf{x}^{\mathbf{n}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m23" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{a\in A:n_{a}&gt;0}n_{a}\mathbf{x}^{\mathbf{n}-\mathbf{e}_{a}}=\sum_{a\in A}\partial_{a}\mathbf{x}^{\mathbf{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>a</mi></msub><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>a</mi></msub><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝐧</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{a\in A:n_{a}&gt;0}n_{a}\mathbf{x}^{\mathbf{n}-\mathbf{e}_{a}}=\sum_{a\in A}\partial_{a}\mathbf{x}^{\mathbf{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, by exchanging the order of the sum above, we have <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\nu}(\mathbf{x})=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{a\in A}\partial_{a}h_{\mu}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\nu}(\mathbf{x})=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{a\in A}\partial_{a}h_{\mu}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lorentzian and <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> is its directional derivative in the direction <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{m}\mathbf{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{m}\mathbf{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem5" title="Proposition 2.5. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a> shows that <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lorentzian. Hence, <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> is Lorentzian.
As <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{\bullet}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∙</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{\bullet}</annotation></semantics></math> is deletion-compatible, <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\supp\nu\subseteq\Omega_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\supp\nu\subseteq\Omega_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math> follows immediately. Therefore, <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu\in\mathcal{N}_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu\in\mathcal{N}_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of <a href="#S3.I1.i2" title="Item (2) ‣ Lemma 3.4. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(2)</span></a>.</span> Fix <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in A</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(X_{m}=a)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(X_{m}=a)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\coloneqq\mathcal{L}(X_{[m-1]}\mid X_{m}=a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\coloneqq\mathcal{L}(X_{[m-1]}\mid X_{m}=a)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is indeed exchangeable on <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Rewrite the count-generating polynomial of <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="S3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle h_{\rho}(\mathbf{x})=\Ex_{X\sim\mu}\bigl[\mathbf{x}^{T(X)-\mathbf{e}_{a}}\mid X_{m}=a\bigr]=\frac{1}{\Pr(X_{m}=a)}\sum_{{\bm{\omega}}\in A^{m}:\omega_{m}=a}\Pr_{X\sim\mu}(X={\bm{\omega}})\,\mathbf{x}^{T({\bm{\omega}})-\mathbf{e}_{a}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{\rho}(\mathbf{x})=\Ex_{X\sim\mu}\bigl[\mathbf{x}^{T(X)-\mathbf{e}_{a}}\mid X_{m}=a\bigr]=\frac{1}{\Pr(X_{m}=a)}\sum_{{\bm{\omega}}\in A^{m}:\omega_{m}=a}\Pr_{X\sim\mu}(X={\bm{\omega}})\,\mathbf{x}^{T({\bm{\omega}})-\mathbf{e}_{a}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S3.E3" title="In Proof. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> again gives</p>
<table id="S3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{{\bm{\omega}}\in A^{m}:\omega_{m}=a}\Pr_{X\sim\mu}(X={\bm{\omega}})\,\mathbf{x}^{T({\bm{\omega}})-\mathbf{e}_{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{{\bm{\omega}}\in A^{m}:\omega_{m}=a}\Pr_{X\sim\mu}(X={\bm{\omega}})\,\mathbf{x}^{T({\bm{\omega}})-\mathbf{e}_{a}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathbf{n}\in\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A):\\
n_{a}&gt;0,\,\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})&gt;0\end{subarray}}\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})\Pr_{X\sim\mu}(X_{m}=a\mid T(X)=\mathbf{n})\,\mathbf{x}^{\mathbf{n}-\mathbf{e}_{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathbf{n}\in\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A):\\
n_{a}&gt;0,\,\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})&gt;0\end{subarray}}\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})\Pr_{X\sim\mu}(X_{m}=a\mid T(X)=\mathbf{n})\,\mathbf{x}^{\mathbf{n}-\mathbf{e}_{a}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
