<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathbf{n}\in\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A):\\
n_{a}&gt;0,\,\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})&gt;0\end{subarray}}\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})\frac{n_{a}}{m}\mathbf{x}^{\mathbf{n}-\mathbf{e}_{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathbf{n}\in\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A):\\
n_{a}&gt;0,\,\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})&gt;0\end{subarray}}\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})\frac{n_{a}}{m}\mathbf{x}^{\mathbf{n}-\mathbf{e}_{a}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{m}\partial_{a}h_{\mu}(\mathbf{x})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{m}\partial_{a}h_{\mu}(\mathbf{x}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lorentzian, <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem5" title="Proposition 2.5. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a> again shows that <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lorentzian. Thus, <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> is Lorentzian.
As <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\supp\rho\subseteq\supp\nu\subseteq\Omega_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\supp\rho\subseteq\supp\nu\subseteq\Omega_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we conclude that <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in\mathcal{N}_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in\mathcal{N}_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we prove a one-coordinate relative entropy contraction for exchangeable laws <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> Lorentzian.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.5</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> be exchangeable laws on <math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> is Lorentzian, then</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\mu_{1}\mathbin{\|}\nu_{1})\leq\frac{1}{m}D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mu_{1}\mathbin{\|}\nu_{1})\leq\frac{1}{m}D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\not\ll\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>≪̸</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\not\ll\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)=+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)=+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, which trivializes the desired inequality. We thus assume <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\ll\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\ll\nu</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">We start by checking <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1}\ll\nu_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≪</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1}\ll\nu_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mu}\ll\pi_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>≪</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mu}\ll\pi_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{1}(a)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{1}(a)=0</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in A</annotation></semantics></math>, then since <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> is exchangeable, <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu({\bm{\omega}})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu({\bm{\omega}})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\omega}}\in A^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\omega}}\in A^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> that contains <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>. From <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\ll\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\ll\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu({\bm{\omega}})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu({\bm{\omega}})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all such <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\omega}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝎</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\omega}}</annotation></semantics></math>, whence <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1}(a)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1}(a)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Similarly, if <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\nu}(\mathbf{n})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\nu}(\mathbf{n})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{n}\in\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{n}\in\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu({\bm{\omega}})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu({\bm{\omega}})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\omega}}\in A^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\omega}}\in A^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> whose count vector is <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐧</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, so again <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu({\bm{\omega}})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu({\bm{\omega}})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all such <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\omega}}\in A^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\omega}}\in A^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in A</annotation></semantics></math>, let</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{a}\coloneqq\Ex_{X\sim\mu}N_{a}(X)=\Ex_{Z\sim\pi_{\mu}}Z(a),\qquad v_{a}\coloneqq\Ex_{Y\sim\nu}N_{a}(Y)=\Ex_{W\sim\pi_{\nu}}W(a)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{a}\coloneqq\Ex_{X\sim\mu}N_{a}(X)=\Ex_{Z\sim\pi_{\mu}}Z(a),\qquad v_{a}\coloneqq\Ex_{Y\sim\nu}N_{a}(Y)=\Ex_{W\sim\pi_{\nu}}W(a).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">In other words, <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the expected numbers of occurrences of the letter <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\sim\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\sim\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
Since <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is exchangeable,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1}(a)=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Pr_{X\sim\mu}(X_{j}=a)=\frac{1}{m}\Ex_{X\sim\mu}N_{a}(X)=\frac{u_{a}}{m}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1}(a)=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Pr_{X\sim\mu}(X_{j}=a)=\frac{1}{m}\Ex_{X\sim\mu}N_{a}(X)=\frac{u_{a}}{m},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">and similarly, <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{1}(a)=v_{a}/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{1}(a)=v_{a}/m</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">We claim that <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)=D(\pi_{\mu}\mathbin{\|}\pi_{\nu})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)=D(\pi_{\mu}\mathbin{\|}\pi_{\nu})</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying the chain rule for relative entropy, <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1 (Chain rule for relative entropy). ‣ 3.1 Entropy and relative entropy ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, gives</span></p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)=D(\pi_{\mu}\mathbin{\|}\pi_{\nu})+\Ex_{Z\sim\pi_{\mu}}D(\mu(\makebox[4.30554pt]{$\cdot$}\!\mid T=Z)\mathbin{\|}\nu(\makebox[4.30554pt]{$\cdot$}\!\mid T=Z))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:4.3pt;" width="4.3pt"><mo>⋅</mo></mpadded><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:4.3pt;" width="4.3pt"><mo>⋅</mo></mpadded><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)=D(\pi_{\mu}\mathbin{\|}\pi_{\nu})+\Ex_{Z\sim\pi_{\mu}}D(\mu(\makebox[4.30554pt]{$\cdot$}\!\mid T=Z)\mathbin{\|}\nu(\makebox[4.30554pt]{$\cdot$}\!\mid T=Z)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mu}\ll\pi_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>≪</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mu}\ll\pi_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math>, the conditional law <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nu(\makebox[4.30554pt]{$\cdot$}\!\mid T=\mathbf{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:4.3pt;" width="4.3pt"><mo>⋅</mo></mpadded><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu(\makebox[4.30554pt]{$\cdot$}\!\mid T=\mathbf{n})</annotation></semantics></math> is well-defined whenever <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mu}(\mathbf{n})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. For every such <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐧</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, exchangeability implies that both <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu(\makebox[4.30554pt]{$\cdot$}\!\mid T=\mathbf{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:4.3pt;" width="4.3pt"><mo>⋅</mo></mpadded><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\makebox[4.30554pt]{$\cdot$}\!\mid T=\mathbf{n})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nu(\makebox[4.30554pt]{$\cdot$}\!\mid T=\mathbf{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:4.3pt;" width="4.3pt"><mo>⋅</mo></mpadded><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu(\makebox[4.30554pt]{$\cdot$}\!\mid T=\mathbf{n})</annotation></semantics></math> are uniform on <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{{\bm{\omega}}\in A^{m}:T({\bm{\omega}})=\mathbf{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{\bm{\omega}}\in A^{m}:T({\bm{\omega}})=\mathbf{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the second term on the right-hand side of (<a href="#S3.E4" title="Equation 3.4 ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>) vanishes, so <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)=D(\pi_{\mu}\mathbin{\|}\pi_{\nu})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)=D(\pi_{\mu}\mathbin{\|}\pi_{\nu})</annotation></semantics></math>. It remains to show</span></p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\mu_{1}\mathbin{\|}\nu_{1})\leq\frac{1}{m}D(\pi_{\mu}\mathbin{\|}\pi_{\nu})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mu_{1}\mathbin{\|}\nu_{1})\leq\frac{1}{m}D(\pi_{\mu}\mathbin{\|}\pi_{\nu}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> be the count-generating polynomial of <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition, <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\nu}(\mathbf{1})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\nu}(\mathbf{1})=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and for <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in A</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{a}h_{\nu}(\mathbf{1})=\Ex_{X\sim\nu}N_{a}(X)=v_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{a}h_{\nu}(\mathbf{1})=\Ex_{X\sim\nu}N_{a}(X)=v_{a}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{a}(h_{\nu}^{1/m})(\mathbf{1})=\frac{1}{m}h_{\nu}(\mathbf{1})^{1/m-1}\partial_{a}h_{\nu}(\mathbf{1})=\frac{1}{m}v_{a}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{a}(h_{\nu}^{1/m})(\mathbf{1})=\frac{1}{m}h_{\nu}(\mathbf{1})^{1/m-1}\partial_{a}h_{\nu}(\mathbf{1})=\frac{1}{m}v_{a}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> is Lorentzian, <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lorentzian, so by <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Proposition 2.4. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>, <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\nu}^{1/m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\nu}^{1/m}</annotation></semantics></math> is concave on the positive orthant. Thus, for <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>A</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{A}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\nu}(\mathbf{x})^{1/m}\leq h_{\nu}(\mathbf{1})^{1/m}+\nabla(h_{\nu}^{1/m})(\mathbf{1})\cdot(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{1})=1+\frac{1}{m}\sum_{a\in A}v_{a}(x_{a}-1)=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{a\in A}v_{a}x_{a}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\nu}(\mathbf{x})^{1/m}\leq h_{\nu}(\mathbf{1})^{1/m}+\nabla(h_{\nu}^{1/m})(\mathbf{1})\cdot(\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{1})=1+\frac{1}{m}\sum_{a\in A}v_{a}(x_{a}-1)=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{a\in A}v_{a}x_{a},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p13.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p13.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the last equality uses <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{a\in A}v_{a}/m=\sum_{a\in A}\nu_{1}(a)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{a\in A}v_{a}/m=\sum_{a\in A}\nu_{1}(a)=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
From the definition of <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Ex_{Z\sim\pi_{\nu}}\prod_{a\in A}x_{a}^{Z(a)}\leq\biggl(\frac{1}{m}\sum_{a\in A}v_{a}x_{a}\biggr)^{\!m}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ex_{Z\sim\pi_{\nu}}\prod_{a\in A}x_{a}^{Z(a)}\leq\biggl(\frac{1}{m}\sum_{a\in A}v_{a}x_{a}\biggr)^{\!m}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, for any <math id="S3.SS2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\eta}}\in\mathbb{R}^{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜼</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>A</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\eta}}\in\mathbb{R}^{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, the variational formula for relative entropy with the function <math id="S3.SS2.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\colon\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A)\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\colon\mathcal{Q}_{m}(A)\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> defined by <math id="S3.SS2.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\mathbf{n})\coloneqq\sum_{a\in A}n_{a}\eta_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\mathbf{n})\coloneqq\sum_{a\in A}n_{a}\eta_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D(\pi_{\mu}\mathbin{\|}\pi_{\nu})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D(\pi_{\mu}\mathbin{\|}\pi_{\nu})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\Ex_{\pi_{\mu}}f-\log\Ex_{\pi_{\nu}}e^{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>f</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\Ex_{\pi_{\mu}}f-\log\Ex_{\pi_{\nu}}e^{f}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{a\in A}\Ex_{Z\sim\pi_{\mu}}Z(a)\eta_{a}-\log\Ex_{Z\sim\pi_{\nu}}\exp\biggl(\,\sum_{a\in A}Z(a)\eta_{a}\biggr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{a\in A}\Ex_{Z\sim\pi_{\mu}}Z(a)\eta_{a}-\log\Ex_{Z\sim\pi_{\nu}}\exp\biggl(\,\sum_{a\in A}Z(a)\eta_{a}\biggr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{a\in A}u_{a}\eta_{a}-\log\Ex_{Z\sim\pi_{\nu}}\exp\biggl(\,\sum_{a\in A}Z(a)\eta_{a}\biggr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{a\in A}u_{a}\eta_{a}-\log\Ex_{Z\sim\pi_{\nu}}\exp\biggl(\,\sum_{a\in A}Z(a)\eta_{a}\biggr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">The expectation inside the logarithm is upper-bounded using (<a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 3.6 ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>) applied with <math id="S3.SS2.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{a}=e^{\eta_{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{a}=e^{\eta_{a}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS2.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in A</annotation></semantics></math>, so</span></p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\pi_{\mu}\mathbin{\|}\pi_{\nu})\geq\sum_{a\in A}u_{a}\eta_{a}-m\log\biggl(\frac{1}{m}\sum_{a\in A}v_{a}e^{\eta_{a}}\biggr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\pi_{\mu}\mathbin{\|}\pi_{\nu})\geq\sum_{a\in A}u_{a}\eta_{a}-m\log\biggl(\frac{1}{m}\sum_{a\in A}v_{a}e^{\eta_{a}}\biggr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, we compute <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\mu_{1}\mathbin{\|}\nu_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mu_{1}\mathbin{\|}\nu_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Again, by the variational formula for relative entropy (<a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 3.1 ‣ 3.1 Entropy and relative entropy ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D(\mu_{1}\mathbin{\|}\nu_{1})=\sup_{f\colon A\to\mathbb{R}}\{\Ex_{\mu_{1}}f-\log\Ex_{\nu_{1}}e^{f}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>f</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\mu_{1}\mathbin{\|}\nu_{1})=\sup_{f\colon A\to\mathbb{R}}\{\Ex_{\mu_{1}}f-\log\Ex_{\nu_{1}}e^{f}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">After reparametrizing the supremum by <math id="S3.SS2.p15.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(f(a):a\in A)\in\mathbb{R}^{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>A</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f(a):a\in A)\in\mathbb{R}^{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, the right-hand side becomes</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{{\bm{\eta}}\in\mathbb{R}^{A}}\biggl\{\sum_{a\in A}\mu_{1}(a)\eta_{a}-\log\biggl(\,\sum_{a\in A}\nu_{1}(a)e^{\eta_{a}}\biggr)\biggr\}=\sup_{{\bm{\eta}}\in\mathbb{R}^{A}}\biggl\{\frac{1}{m}\sum_{a\in A}u_{a}\eta_{a}-\log\biggl(\frac{1}{m}\sum_{a\in A}v_{a}e^{\eta_{a}}\biggr)\biggr\}\leq\frac{1}{m}D(\pi_{\mu}\mathbin{\|}\pi_{\nu})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝜼</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>A</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝜼</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>A</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{{\bm{\eta}}\in\mathbb{R}^{A}}\biggl\{\sum_{a\in A}\mu_{1}(a)\eta_{a}-\log\biggl(\,\sum_{a\in A}\nu_{1}(a)e^{\eta_{a}}\biggr)\biggr\}=\sup_{{\bm{\eta}}\in\mathbb{R}^{A}}\biggl\{\frac{1}{m}\sum_{a\in A}u_{a}\eta_{a}-\log\biggl(\frac{1}{m}\sum_{a\in A}v_{a}e^{\eta_{a}}\biggr)\biggr\}\leq\frac{1}{m}D(\pi_{\mu}\mathbin{\|}\pi_{\nu}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p15.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p15.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the inequality follows from (<a href="#S3.E7" title="Equation 3.7 ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a>). This proves (<a href="#S3.E5" title="Equation 3.5 ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>) and completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 3.6</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 3.5. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a> can also be obtained by using entropic independence <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, Theorem 4]</cite> through polarization.
To sketch briefly, our count-generating functions <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> can be multilinearized by replacing each <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in A</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> labeled copies <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1},a_{2},\dots,a_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1},a_{2},\dots,a_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> with a suitable normalization to give laws <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{A\times[m]}{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{A\times[m]}{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. For instance, <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{a}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{a}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is replaced by <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{m}{k}^{-1}\sum_{K\in\binom{[m]}{k}}\prod_{i\in K}x_{a_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{m}{k}^{-1}\sum_{K\in\binom{[m]}{k}}\prod_{i\in K}x_{a_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since this polarization preserves the Lorentzian property <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, Proposition 3.1]</cite>, the generating polynomial of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lorentzian and hence log-concave, so <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> is entropically independent. Because <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> are exchangeable, these lifts satisfy <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(\widetilde{\mu}\mathbin{\|}\widetilde{\nu})=D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\widetilde{\mu}\mathbin{\|}\widetilde{\nu})=D(\mu\mathbin{\|}\nu)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The one-element down marginals, obtained by choosing a uniformly random element of the lifted <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-set, are <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1}\otimes u_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1}\otimes u_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{1}\otimes u_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{1}\otimes u_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, where <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is the uniform law on <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[m]</annotation></semantics></math>. The <math id="S3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{m}</annotation></semantics></math>-contraction for this operation therefore gives the lemma.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p16.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we prove a strengthening of a special case of Shearer’s inequality for exchangeable Lorentzian laws.
For a random vector <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=(X_{1},\dots,X_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=(X_{1},\dots,X_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, Shearer’s inequality states that if <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> is a family of subsets of <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[m]</annotation></semantics></math> such that each <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to at least <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> members of <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="S3.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{G\in\mathcal{G}}\Ent(X_{i}:i\in G)-k\Ent(X)\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{G\in\mathcal{G}}\Ent(X_{i}:i\in G)-k\Ent(X)\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p16.2" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of the <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-subsets of <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[m]</annotation></semantics></math>, the inequality becomes</p>
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{[m]\setminus j})-(m-1)\Ent(X)\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{[m]\setminus j})-(m-1)\Ent(X)\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p16.3" class="ltx_p">This is also called the delete-one case of Han’s inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>, which predates Shearer’s inequality; see also <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, Chapter 17]</cite>.
We strengthen this for <math id="S3.SS2.p16.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\mu\in\mathcal{N}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\mu\in\mathcal{N}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> by showing that</p>
<table id="S3.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{[m]\setminus j})-(m-1)\Ent(X)\geq\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{j})-\Ent(X);" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{[m]\setminus j})-(m-1)\Ent(X)\geq\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{j})-\Ent(X);</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p16.4" class="ltx_p">the right-hand side is nonnegative by subadditivity of entropy.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.7</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="S3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\mu\in\mathcal{N}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\mu\in\mathcal{N}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{[m]\setminus j})\geq(m-2)\Ent(X)+\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{j})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{[m]\setminus j})\geq(m-2)\Ent(X)+\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">We proceed by induction on <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>.
The base case <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=2</annotation></semantics></math> holds with equality.
Assume <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> and let</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
