<p id="S3.SS2.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">so that our goal is to show <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{m}(X)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{m}(X)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Write <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\coloneqq X_{[m-1]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\coloneqq X_{[m-1]}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\coloneqq X_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\coloneqq X_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{[m]\setminus j})=\Ent(Y)+\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}\Ent(Y_{[m-1]\setminus i},Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{[m]\setminus j})=\Ent(Y)+\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}\Ent(Y_{[m-1]\setminus i},Z)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{j})=\Ent(Z)+\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}\Ent(Y_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{j})=\Ent(Z)+\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}\Ent(Y_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substituting these into (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 3.9 ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.9</span></a>) gives</span></p>
