<p id="S3.SS2.p17.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p17.4.1" class="ltx_text">By <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 3.4. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, for every <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(Z=z)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(Z=z)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the conditional law <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(Y\mid Z=z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(Y\mid Z=z)</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the induction hypothesis gives</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Ex_{Z}\Delta_{m-1}(Y\mid Z)\geq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ex_{Z}\Delta_{m-1}(Y\mid Z)\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p17.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p17.5.1" class="ltx_text">so it remains to show</span></p>
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}\mI(Y_{i};Z)\leq\mI(Y;Z)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}\mI(Y_{i};Z)\leq\mI(Y;Z).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p17.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p17.6.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu\coloneqq\mathcal{L}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu\coloneqq\mathcal{L}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>, and for every <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(Z=z)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(Z=z)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{z}\coloneqq\mathcal{L}(Y\mid Z=z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{z}\coloneqq\mathcal{L}(Y\mid Z=z)</annotation></semantics></math>. <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 3.4. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a> implies that both <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> belong to <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 3.2 (Mutual information as relative entropy). ‣ 3.1 Entropy and relative entropy ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> and exchangeability of <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> give</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}\mI(Y_{i};Z)=\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}\Ex_{Z}[D((\rho_{Z})_{i}\mathbin{\|}\nu_{i})]=(m-1)\Ex_{Z}[D((\rho_{Z})_{1}\mathbin{\|}\nu_{1})]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}\mI(Y_{i};Z)=\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}\Ex_{Z}[D((\rho_{Z})_{i}\mathbin{\|}\nu_{i})]=(m-1)\Ex_{Z}[D((\rho_{Z})_{1}\mathbin{\|}\nu_{1})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p17.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p17.7.1" class="ltx_text">For every such <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 3.5. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a> implies <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D((\rho_{z})_{1}\mathbin{\|}\nu_{1})\leq\frac{1}{m-1}D(\rho_{z}\mathbin{\|}\nu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D((\rho_{z})_{1}\mathbin{\|}\nu_{1})\leq\frac{1}{m-1}D(\rho_{z}\mathbin{\|}\nu)</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 3.2 (Mutual information as relative entropy). ‣ 3.1 Entropy and relative entropy ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> again gives <math id="S3.SS2.p17.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mI(Y;Z)=\Ex_{Z}[D(\rho_{Z}\mathbin{\|}\nu)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mI(Y;Z)=\Ex_{Z}[D(\rho_{Z}\mathbin{\|}\nu)]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Combining these yields (<a href="#S3.E10" title="Equation 3.10 ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.10</span></a>), completing the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 3.8</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since each <math id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{[m]\setminus j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{[m]\setminus j}</annotation></semantics></math> is a function of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Ent(X_{[m]\setminus j})\leq\Ent(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ent(X_{[m]\setminus j})\leq\Ent(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using this with <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma 3.7. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a> implies that for every finite set of letters <math id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\mu\in\mathcal{N}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\mu\in\mathcal{N}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Ent(X)\geq\frac{1}{2}\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{j})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ent(X)\geq\frac{1}{2}\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, identify <math id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> with the random subset <math id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{X}\coloneqq\{j\in[m]:X_{j}=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{X}\coloneqq\{j\in[m]:X_{j}=1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> be the law of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Following Anari–Oveis Gharan–Vinzant <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>, a law <math id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{[m]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{[m]}</annotation></semantics></math> is called <em id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">log-concave</em> if its multiaffine generating polynomial <math id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\theta}(\mathbf{z})\coloneqq\sum_{S\subseteq[m]}\theta(S)\prod_{i\in S}z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\theta}(\mathbf{z})\coloneqq\sum_{S\subseteq[m]}\theta(S)\prod_{i\in S}z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is log-concave on the positive orthant.
In the present exchangeable Lorentzian setting, polarization shows that both <math id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> and its complementary law <math id="S3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho^{\ast}(S)\coloneqq\rho([m]\setminus S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho^{\ast}(S)\coloneqq\rho([m]\setminus S)</annotation></semantics></math> are log-concave.
Hence, (<a href="#S3.E11" title="Equation 3.11 ‣ Remark 3.8. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.11</span></a>) also follows from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, Corollary 5.6]</cite>.
Thus, under our stronger exchangeable Lorentzian hypothesis, <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma 3.7. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a> refines (<a href="#S3.E11" title="Equation 3.11 ‣ Remark 3.8. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.11</span></a>) to a delete-one entropy inequality applicable to an arbitrary finite set of letters.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Optimized pressure and its monotonicity</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now convert the entropy estimates from <a href="#S3" title="3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> into an abstract monotonicity principle for extremal logarithmic values of partition functions, which we call the optimized pressure<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
          This terminology is motivated by the statistical-mechanical interpretation of the logarithm of a partition function, up to normalization, as a pressure; see, e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, Chapter 3]</cite>.</span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite set of letters. Let <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Omega_{\bullet}=(\Omega_{m}:m\geq 1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∙</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{\bullet}=(\Omega_{m}:m\geq 1)</annotation></semantics></math> be a support family which is permutation-invariant and deletion-compatible. Assume each <math id="S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is nonempty.
For each <math id="S4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> be the family of laws on <math id="S4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Denote by <math id="S4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{m}\coloneqq\mathcal{N}_{m}(\Omega_{\bullet})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∙</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{m}\coloneqq\mathcal{N}_{m}(\Omega_{\bullet})</annotation></semantics></math> the families of exchangeable laws and exchangeable Lorentzian laws on <math id="S4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. In particular, <math id="S4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{m}\subseteq\mathcal{E}_{m}\subseteq\mathcal{L}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{m}\subseteq\mathcal{E}_{m}\subseteq\mathcal{L}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. Whenever <math id="S4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{L}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{L}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, write <math id="S4.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=(X_{1},\dots,X_{m})\sim\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=(X_{1},\dots,X_{m})\sim\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{m}\colon\Omega_{m}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{m}\colon\Omega_{m}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a permutation-invariant energy function, meaning that <math id="S4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{m}(\omega_{\pi(1)},\dots,\omega_{\pi(m)})=U_{m}({\bm{\omega}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{m}(\omega_{\pi(1)},\dots,\omega_{\pi(m)})=U_{m}({\bm{\omega}})</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and every permutation <math id="S4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[m]</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)</annotation></semantics></math> be the family of positive laws on <math id="S4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</p>
<table id="S4.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)\coloneqq\biggl\{\alpha\colon A\to\mathbb{R}^{+}:\sum_{a\in A}\alpha(a)=1\biggr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)\coloneqq\biggl\{\alpha\colon A\to\mathbb{R}^{+}:\sum_{a\in A}\alpha(a)=1\biggr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="S4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{m}(\alpha)\coloneqq\sum_{{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}}\exp(U_{m}({\bm{\omega}}))\prod_{j=1}^{m}\alpha(\omega_{j})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{m}(\alpha)\coloneqq\sum_{{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}}\exp(U_{m}({\bm{\omega}}))\prod_{j=1}^{m}\alpha(\omega_{j}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.3" class="ltx_p">and the <em id="S4.p3.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">optimized pressure</em></p>
<table id="S4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{m}\coloneqq\sup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)}\log\mathcal{Z}_{m}(\alpha)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{m}\coloneqq\sup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)}\log\mathcal{Z}_{m}(\alpha).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.4" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>, define a law <math id="S4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{m}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{m}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S4.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="S4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{m}^{\alpha}({\bm{\omega}})\coloneqq\frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}_{m}(\alpha)}\exp(U_{m}({\bm{\omega}}))\prod_{j=1}^{m}\alpha(\omega_{j})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{m}^{\alpha}({\bm{\omega}})\coloneqq\frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}_{m}(\alpha)}\exp(U_{m}({\bm{\omega}}))\prod_{j=1}^{m}\alpha(\omega_{j}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.5" class="ltx_p">which is exchangeable since <math id="S4.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> are permutation-invariant.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The following properties are possessed by some particular choices of <math id="S4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. We first derive consequences of these properties and later verify them for our specific choice of <math id="S4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. More precisely, in <a href="#S5.SS2" title="5.2 Resolution of the local membership problem ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>, we verify <a href="#S4.I1.i1" title="Item (1) ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(1)</span></a> for antiferromagnetic models using the Lorentzian property of the partition function and verify <a href="#S4.Ex5" title="Item (2) ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(2)</span></a> by a simple counting argument.</p>
<ol id="S4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{m}^{\alpha}\in\mathcal{N}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{m}^{\alpha}\in\mathcal{N}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The energy function satisfies the deletion identity: for <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{m}U_{m-1}({\bm{\omega}}_{[m]\setminus j})=(m-2)U_{m}({\bm{\omega}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝎</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{m}U_{m-1}({\bm{\omega}}_{[m]\setminus j})=(m-2)U_{m}({\bm{\omega}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <a href="#S4.I1.i1" title="Item (1) ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(1)</span></a>. Then for <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{m}=\sup_{\mu\in\mathcal{N}_{m}}\biggl\{\Ex_{\mu}U_{m}(X)+\Ent(X)-\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{j})\biggr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{m}=\sup_{\mu\in\mathcal{N}_{m}}\biggl\{\Ex_{\mu}U_{m}(X)+\Ent(X)-\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{j})\biggr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, we represent <math id="S4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> as a supremum taken over <math id="S4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then applying the Gibbs variational formula, <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Gibbs variational formula). ‣ 3.1 Entropy and relative entropy ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, to</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\alpha}({\bm{\omega}})\coloneqq U_{m}({\bm{\omega}})+\sum_{j=1}^{m}\log\alpha(\omega_{j})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\alpha}({\bm{\omega}})\coloneqq U_{m}({\bm{\omega}})+\sum_{j=1}^{m}\log\alpha(\omega_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log\sum_{{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}}\exp(U_{m}({\bm{\omega}}))\prod_{j=1}^{m}\alpha(\omega_{j})=\sup_{\mu\in\mathcal{L}_{m}}\biggl\{\Ex_{\mu}U_{m}(X)+\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ex_{\mu}\log\alpha(X_{j})+\Ent(X)\biggr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\sum_{{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}}\exp(U_{m}({\bm{\omega}}))\prod_{j=1}^{m}\alpha(\omega_{j})=\sup_{\mu\in\mathcal{L}_{m}}\biggl\{\Ex_{\mu}U_{m}(X)+\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ex_{\mu}\log\alpha(X_{j})+\Ent(X)\biggr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">After taking the supremum over <math id="S4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>, the left-hand side equals <math id="S4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> by definition, so</span></p>
<table id="S4.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{m}=\sup_{\mu\in\mathcal{L}_{m}}\biggl\{\Ex_{\mu}U_{m}(X)+\sup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)}\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ex_{\mu}\log\alpha(X_{j})+\Ent(X)\biggr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{m}=\sup_{\mu\in\mathcal{L}_{m}}\biggl\{\Ex_{\mu}U_{m}(X)+\sup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)}\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ex_{\mu}\log\alpha(X_{j})+\Ent(X)\biggr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Second, we prove the analogue of (<a href="#S4.E1" title="Equation 4.1 ‣ Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>) with <math id="S4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="S4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{L}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{L}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mu}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mu}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> be its average one-site marginal:</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\coloneqq\frac{1}{m}\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Pr_{X\sim\mu}(X_{j}=a),\qquad a\in A." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\coloneqq\frac{1}{m}\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Pr_{X\sim\mu}(X_{j}=a),\qquad a\in A.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then, for <math id="S4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ex_{\mu}\log\alpha(X_{j})=m\sum_{a\in A}\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\log\alpha(a)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ex_{\mu}\log\alpha(X_{j})=m\sum_{a\in A}\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\log\alpha(a).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the supremum over <math id="S4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)}\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ex_{\mu}\log\alpha(X_{j})=m\sup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)}\sum_{a\in A}\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\log\alpha(a)=m\sum_{a\in A}\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\log\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)=-m\Ent(\bar{\mu}_{1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)}\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ex_{\mu}\log\alpha(X_{j})=m\sup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)}\sum_{a\in A}\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\log\alpha(a)=m\sum_{a\in A}\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\log\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)=-m\Ent(\bar{\mu}_{1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">To justify the second equality, note that <math id="S4.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mu}_{1}\ll\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≪</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mu}_{1}\ll\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S4.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, nonnegativity of relative entropy yields</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{a\in A}\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\log\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)-\sum_{a\in A}\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\log\alpha(a)=D(\bar{\mu}_{1}\mathbin{\|}\alpha)\geq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{a\in A}\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\log\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)-\sum_{a\in A}\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\log\alpha(a)=D(\bar{\mu}_{1}\mathbin{\|}\alpha)\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">where equality occurs if <math id="S4.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\bar{\mu}_{1}\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\bar{\mu}_{1}\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, if <math id="S4.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mu}_{1}\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mu}_{1}\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)}\sum_{a\in A}\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\log\alpha(a)=\sum_{a\in A}\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\log\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)}\sum_{a\in A}\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\log\alpha(a)=\sum_{a\in A}\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\log\bar{\mu}_{1}(a).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p6.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p6.6.1" class="ltx_text">Even if <math id="S4.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mu}_{1}\notin\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mu}_{1}\notin\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)</annotation></semantics></math> in general, let <math id="S4.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> be the uniform law on <math id="S4.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and consider <math id="S4.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\varepsilon}\coloneqq(1-\varepsilon)\bar{\mu}_{1}+\varepsilon u\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\varepsilon}\coloneqq(1-\varepsilon)\bar{\mu}_{1}+\varepsilon u\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S4.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{a\in A}\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\log\alpha_{\varepsilon}(a)\to\sum_{a\in A}\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\log\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\quad\text{as}\quad\varepsilon\to 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>as</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{a\in A}\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\log\alpha_{\varepsilon}(a)\to\sum_{a\in A}\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\log\bar{\mu}_{1}(a)\quad\text{as}\quad\varepsilon\to 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p6.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p6.7.1" class="ltx_text">with the convention <math id="S4.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\log 0=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\log 0=0</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies (<a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4.4 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>), whence (<a href="#S4.E3" title="Equation 4.3 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>) follows.
Substituting (<a href="#S4.E3" title="Equation 4.3 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>) into (<a href="#S4.E2" title="Equation 4.2 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{m}=\sup_{\mu\in\mathcal{L}_{m}}\{\Ex_{\mu}U_{m}(X)+\Ent(X)-m\Ent(\bar{\mu}_{1})\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{m}=\sup_{\mu\in\mathcal{L}_{m}}\{\Ex_{\mu}U_{m}(X)+\Ent(X)-m\Ent(\bar{\mu}_{1})\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{L}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{L}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\mathrm{sym}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>sym</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\mathrm{sym}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the symmetrization of <math id="S4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> over all permutations of the <math id="S4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> sites, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\mathrm{sym}}\coloneqq\frac{1}{m!}\sum_{\pi\in\mathfrak{S}_{m}}\mu^{(\pi)},\qquad\mu^{(\pi)}(\omega_{1},\dots,\omega_{m})\coloneqq\mu(\omega_{\pi(1)},\dots,\omega_{\pi(m)})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>sym</mi></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\mathrm{sym}}\coloneqq\frac{1}{m!}\sum_{\pi\in\mathfrak{S}_{m}}\mu^{(\pi)},\qquad\mu^{(\pi)}(\omega_{1},\dots,\omega_{m})\coloneqq\mu(\omega_{\pi(1)},\dots,\omega_{\pi(m)}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{S}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{S}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is the symmetric group on <math id="S4.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[m]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="S4.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\mathrm{sym}}\in\mathcal{E}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>sym</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\mathrm{sym}}\in\mathcal{E}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, and permutation invariance of <math id="S4.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="S4.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Ex_{\mu^{\mathrm{sym}}}U_{m}=\Ex_{\mu}U_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>sym</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ex_{\mu^{\mathrm{sym}}}U_{m}=\Ex_{\mu}U_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. By concavity of entropy,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Ent(\mu^{{\mathrm{sym}}})\geq\frac{1}{m!}\sum_{\pi\in\mathfrak{S}_{m}}\Ent(\mu^{(\pi)})=\Ent(\mu)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>sym</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔖</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ent(\mu^{{\mathrm{sym}}})\geq\frac{1}{m!}\sum_{\pi\in\mathfrak{S}_{m}}\Ent(\mu^{(\pi)})=\Ent(\mu).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, <math id="S4.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mu^{\mathrm{sym}})_{1}=\bar{\mu}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>sym</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mu^{\mathrm{sym}})_{1}=\bar{\mu}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S4.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Ent((\mu^{\mathrm{sym}})_{1})=\Ent(\bar{\mu}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>sym</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ent((\mu^{\mathrm{sym}})_{1})=\Ent(\bar{\mu}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, symmetrization does not decrease the objective in (<a href="#S4.E5" title="Equation 4.5 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>). If <math id="S4.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is exchangeable and <math id="S4.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Ent(\bar{\mu}_{1})=\Ent(X_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ent(\bar{\mu}_{1})=\Ent(X_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence,</span></p>
<table id="S4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{m}=\sup_{\mu\in\mathcal{E}_{m}}\biggl\{\Ex_{\mu}U_{m}(X)+\Ent(X)-\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{j})\biggr\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{m}=\sup_{\mu\in\mathcal{E}_{m}}\biggl\{\Ex_{\mu}U_{m}(X)+\Ent(X)-\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{j})\biggr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">which is the desired analogue of (<a href="#S4.E1" title="Equation 4.1 ‣ Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, we show (<a href="#S4.E1" title="Equation 4.1 ‣ Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>).
Fix <math id="S4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\mu_{m}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\mu_{m}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{m}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{m}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Gibbs law associated with <math id="S4.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, the Gibbs variational formula for <math id="S4.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Gibbs variational formula). ‣ 3.1 Entropy and relative entropy ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> with <math id="S4.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=f^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=f^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Ex_{\mu_{m}^{\alpha}}\biggl(U_{m}(X)+\sum_{j=1}^{m}\log\alpha(X_{j})\biggr)+\Ent(\mu_{m}^{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Ex_{\mu_{m}^{\alpha}}\biggl(U_{m}(X)+\sum_{j=1}^{m}\log\alpha(X_{j})\biggr)+\Ent(\mu_{m}^{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad=\log\sum_{{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}}e^{f^{\alpha}({\bm{\omega}})}=\log\sum_{{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}}\exp(U_{m}({\bm{\omega}}))\prod_{j=1}^{m}\alpha(\omega_{j})=\log\mathcal{Z}_{m}(\alpha)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad=\log\sum_{{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}}e^{f^{\alpha}({\bm{\omega}})}=\log\sum_{{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}}\exp(U_{m}({\bm{\omega}}))\prod_{j=1}^{m}\alpha(\omega_{j})=\log\mathcal{Z}_{m}(\alpha).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Adding <math id="S4.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{m}D((\mu_{m}^{\alpha})_{j}\mathbin{\|}\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{m}D((\mu_{m}^{\alpha})_{j}\mathbin{\|}\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> to both sides and using <math id="S4.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D((\mu_{m}^{\alpha})_{j}\mathbin{\|}\alpha)=\Ex_{\mu_{m}^{\alpha}}\log\frac{(\mu_{m}^{\alpha})_{j}(X_{j})}{\alpha(X_{j})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D((\mu_{m}^{\alpha})_{j}\mathbin{\|}\alpha)=\Ex_{\mu_{m}^{\alpha}}\log\frac{(\mu_{m}^{\alpha})_{j}(X_{j})}{\alpha(X_{j})}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Ex_{\mu_{m}^{\alpha}}U_{m}(X)+\Ent(\mu_{m}^{\alpha})-\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent((\mu_{m}^{\alpha})_{j})=\log\mathcal{Z}_{m}(\alpha)+\sum_{j=1}^{m}D((\mu_{m}^{\alpha})_{j}\mathbin{\|}\alpha)\geq\log\mathcal{Z}_{m}(\alpha)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∥</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ex_{\mu_{m}^{\alpha}}U_{m}(X)+\Ent(\mu_{m}^{\alpha})-\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent((\mu_{m}^{\alpha})_{j})=\log\mathcal{Z}_{m}(\alpha)+\sum_{j=1}^{m}D((\mu_{m}^{\alpha})_{j}\mathbin{\|}\alpha)\geq\log\mathcal{Z}_{m}(\alpha).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the supremum over <math id="S4.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)</annotation></semantics></math> and using <math id="S4.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{m}^{\alpha}\in\mathcal{N}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{m}^{\alpha}\in\mathcal{N}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> from <a href="#S4.I1.i1" title="Item (1) ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(1)</span></a> gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\mu\in\mathcal{N}_{m}}\biggl\{\Ex_{\mu}U_{m}(X)+\Ent(X)-\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{j})\biggr\}\geq\sup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)}\log\mathcal{Z}_{m}(\alpha)=F_{m}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\mu\in\mathcal{N}_{m}}\biggl\{\Ex_{\mu}U_{m}(X)+\Ent(X)-\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{j})\biggr\}\geq\sup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)}\log\mathcal{Z}_{m}(\alpha)=F_{m}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">The reverse inequality follows from <math id="S4.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{m}\subseteq\mathcal{E}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{m}\subseteq\mathcal{E}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and (<a href="#S4.E6" title="Equation 4.6 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.6</span></a>), which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Using <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemmas</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma 3.7. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a>, together with closure properties of Lorentzian laws in <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 3.4. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, we derive a monotonicity principle for <math id="S4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> given the aforementioned properties.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4.2</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <a href="#S4.I1.i1" title="Item (1) ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(1)</span></a> and <a href="#S4.Ex5" title="Item (2) ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(2)</span></a>. Then for <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="mF_{m-1}\geq(m-2)F_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">mF_{m-1}\geq(m-2)F_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be arbitrary. Using <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, choose <math id="S4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{N}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{N}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S4.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{m}-\varepsilon\leq\Ex_{\mu}U_{m}(X)+\Ent(X)-\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{j})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{m}-\varepsilon\leq\Ex_{\mu}U_{m}(X)+\Ent(X)-\sum_{j=1}^{m}\Ent(X_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">For each <math id="S4.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 3.4. ‣ 3.2 Exchangeable Lorentzian laws and entropy contraction ‣ 3 Entropy inequalities for exchangeable Lorentzian laws ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a> implies that the law of <math id="S4.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{[m]\setminus j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{[m]\setminus j}</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to <math id="S4.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, applying <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> with <math id="S4.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="S4.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m-1</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
