<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We are ready to prove <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 1.2. ‣ 1.1 A vertex-inhomogeneous strengthening ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>.
Throughout this section, we fix an antiferromagnetic model <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> on a finite nonempty spin set <math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall that <math id="S5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{G}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{Z}_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>G</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Z}_{G}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the vertex-homogeneous and vertex-inhomogeneous partition functions, respectively, i.e.,</p>
<table id="S5.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{Z}_{G}({\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)}:v\in V(G))=\sum_{{\bm{\sigma}}\in I^{V(G)}}\prod_{uv\in E(G)}H(\sigma_{u},\sigma_{v})\prod_{v\in V(G)}\lambda^{(v)}_{\sigma_{v}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>G</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Z}_{G}({\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)}:v\in V(G))=\sum_{{\bm{\sigma}}\in I^{V(G)}}\prod_{uv\in E(G)}H(\sigma_{u},\sigma_{v})\prod_{v\in V(G)}\lambda^{(v)}_{\sigma_{v}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and <math id="S5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{G}({\bm{\lambda}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{G}({\bm{\lambda}})</annotation></semantics></math> is the function <math id="S5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{Z}_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>G</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Z}_{G}</annotation></semantics></math> evaluated with <math id="S5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)}={\bm{\lambda}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝝀</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)}={\bm{\lambda}}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V(G)</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="S5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in I</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the row of <math id="S5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> indexed by <math id="S5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>. By continuity with respect to the fugacity vectors, it suffices to consider the case when every fugacity vector is entrywise positive.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We prove by induction on <math id="S5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=v(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=v(G)</annotation></semantics></math> that (<a href="#S1.E2" title="Equation 1.2 ‣ Theorem 1.2. ‣ 1.1 A vertex-inhomogeneous strengthening ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>) holds for every antiferromagnetic model <math id="S5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> and every collection of positive fugacity vectors. The cases <math id="S5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1</annotation></semantics></math> are immediate. For the induction step, we may assume that <math id="S5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is connected, since both sides of (<a href="#S1.E2" title="Equation 1.2 ‣ Theorem 1.2. ‣ 1.1 A vertex-inhomogeneous strengthening ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>) factor over connected components of <math id="S5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, we may assume that <math id="S5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> has no isolated vertices. If <math id="S5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is the zero matrix, both sides vanish. Otherwise, delete the zero rows and corresponding columns of <math id="S5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> and restrict the fugacity vectors to the remaining spins. This leaves both sides unchanged and produces a nonempty antiferromagnetic model with no zero rows. Therefore, we may assume that <math id="S5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> has no zero rows.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">By <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Corollary 2.3. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Corollary</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>, <math id="S5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is irreducible. Hence, by the Perron–Frobenius theorem (<a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2 (Perron–Frobenius). ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>), <math id="S5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> has an eigenvalue <math id="S5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> with a corresponding entrywise-positive eigenvector <math id="S5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Normalize <math id="S5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="S5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\mathbf{r}\rVert_{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>𝐫</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\mathbf{r}\rVert_{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is antiferromagnetic, <math id="S5.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> is its unique positive eigenvalue. Then for <math id="S5.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{(\varepsilon)}\coloneqq H+\varepsilon\mathbf{r}\mathbf{r}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐫𝐫</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{(\varepsilon)}\coloneqq H+\varepsilon\mathbf{r}\mathbf{r}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is entrywise positive. We claim that <math id="S5.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{(\varepsilon)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{(\varepsilon)}</annotation></semantics></math> is antiferromagnetic. Since <math id="S5.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetric, choose an orthonormal eigenbasis <math id="S5.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> containing <math id="S5.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for <math id="S5.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}\in\mathcal{B}\setminus\{\mathbf{r}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}\in\mathcal{B}\setminus\{\mathbf{r}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{(\varepsilon)}\mathbf{u}=H\mathbf{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{(\varepsilon)}\mathbf{u}=H\mathbf{u}</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="S5.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{(\varepsilon)}\mathbf{r}=H\mathbf{r}+\varepsilon\mathbf{r}=(\rho+\varepsilon)\mathbf{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐫</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐫</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐫</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐫</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{(\varepsilon)}\mathbf{r}=H\mathbf{r}+\varepsilon\mathbf{r}=(\rho+\varepsilon)\mathbf{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the spectrum of <math id="S5.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{(\varepsilon)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{(\varepsilon)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the same as that of <math id="S5.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> except that the eigenvalue <math id="S5.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> is replaced by <math id="S5.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho+\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho+\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S5.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> is the unique positive eigenvalue of <math id="S5.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="S5.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{(\varepsilon)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{(\varepsilon)}</annotation></semantics></math> is antiferromagnetic.
Both sides of (<a href="#S1.E2" title="Equation 1.2 ‣ Theorem 1.2. ‣ 1.1 A vertex-inhomogeneous strengthening ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>) are continuous with respect to the entries of <math id="S5.p3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, so proving the inequality for <math id="S5.p3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{(\varepsilon)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{(\varepsilon)}</annotation></semantics></math> and then letting <math id="S5.p3.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> concludes its proof. Hence, in what follows in this section, we assume that <math id="S5.p3.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is entrywise positive.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Inductive localization and the dual set</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we reduce the problem to a membership problem which depends only on a maximum degree vertex and its neighbors.
As explained in <a href="#S1.SS4" title="1.4 Proof strategy ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.4</span></a>, this part follows the argument in our previous work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>.
We also note that the assumption that <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is antiferromagnetic is not used in this subsection.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Fixing a vertex <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> of maximum degree <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> and conditioning on its spin, we obtain a recurrence relation for the vertex-inhomogeneous partition functions (<a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 5.1. ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>).
Applying the induction hypothesis and canceling from the desired inequality the common terms corresponding to vertices in <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(G)\setminus(\{w\}\cup N(w))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(G)\setminus(\{w\}\cup N(w))</annotation></semantics></math>, we reduce the problem to a local inequality on <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> and its neighbors, as given in (<a href="#S5.E3" title="Equation 5.3 ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>).
To eliminate the dependence on <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\lambda}}^{(w)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\lambda}}^{(w)}</annotation></semantics></math> in this local inequality, we consider its equivalent form in (<a href="#S5.E4" title="Equation 5.4 ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>), which is a membership problem for the set <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, the dual set associated with the normalized clique partition function <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Z_{\Delta+1})^{1/(\Delta+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z_{\Delta+1})^{1/(\Delta+1)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Utilizing log-convexity of <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 5.2. ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>), we reduce this problem to a local membership problem (<a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 5.3. ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>), which we prove in the subsequent subsection.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We start by establishing a recurrence relation for the vertex-inhomogeneous partition functions, which generalizes the well-known identity <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i(G)=i(G\setminus w)+i(G\setminus(N(w)\cup\{w\}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i(G)=i(G\setminus w)+i(G\setminus(N(w)\cup\{w\}))</annotation></semantics></math> for independent set counts.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.1</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝛌</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V(G)</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in V(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in V(G)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{Z}_{G}({\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)}:v\in V(G))=\sum_{\sigma\in I}\lambda^{(w)}_{\sigma}\widetilde{Z}_{G\setminus w}({\bm{\mu}}^{(v,\sigma)}:v\in V(G\setminus w))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>G</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Z}_{G}({\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)}:v\in V(G))=\sum_{\sigma\in I}\lambda^{(w)}_{\sigma}\widetilde{Z}_{G\setminus w}({\bm{\mu}}^{(v,\sigma)}:v\in V(G\setminus w)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where for <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V(G\setminus w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V(G\setminus w)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\mu}}^{(v,\sigma)}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝛍</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\mu}}^{(v,\sigma)}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝛌</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\notin N(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\notin N(w)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot{\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>𝛌</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot{\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in N(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in N(w)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{Z}_{G}({\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)}:v\in V(G))=\sum_{{\bm{\eta}}\colon V(G)\to I}\prod_{uv\in E(G)}H(\eta_{u},\eta_{v})\prod_{v\in V(G)}\lambda^{(v)}_{\eta_{v}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>G</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝜼</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Z}_{G}({\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)}:v\in V(G))=\sum_{{\bm{\eta}}\colon V(G)\to I}\prod_{uv\in E(G)}H(\eta_{u},\eta_{v})\prod_{v\in V(G)}\lambda^{(v)}_{\eta_{v}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">We partition the sum according to the spin assigned to <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in I</annotation></semantics></math>, and consider an assignment <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\eta}}\colon V(G)\to I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜼</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\eta}}\colon V(G)\to I</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{w}=\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{w}=\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\tau}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝉</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\tau}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote its restriction to <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(G\setminus w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(G\setminus w)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\prod_{uv\in E(G)}H(\eta_{u},\eta_{v})\prod_{v\in V(G)}\lambda^{(v)}_{\eta_{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\prod_{uv\in E(G)}H(\eta_{u},\eta_{v})\prod_{v\in V(G)}\lambda^{(v)}_{\eta_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lambda^{(w)}_{\sigma}\Biggl(\,\prod_{uv\in E(G\setminus w)}H(\tau_{u},\tau_{v})\Biggr)\Biggl(\,\prod_{v\in N(w)}H(\sigma,\tau_{v})\Biggr)\Biggl(\,\prod_{v\in V(G\setminus w)}\lambda^{(v)}_{\tau_{v}}\Biggr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lambda^{(w)}_{\sigma}\Biggl(\,\prod_{uv\in E(G\setminus w)}H(\tau_{u},\tau_{v})\Biggr)\Biggl(\,\prod_{v\in N(w)}H(\sigma,\tau_{v})\Biggr)\Biggl(\,\prod_{v\in V(G\setminus w)}\lambda^{(v)}_{\tau_{v}}\Biggr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lambda^{(w)}_{\sigma}\Biggl(\,\prod_{uv\in E(G\setminus w)}H(\tau_{u},\tau_{v})\Biggr)\Biggl(\,\prod_{v\in V(G\setminus w)}\mu^{(v,\sigma)}_{\tau_{v}}\Biggr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lambda^{(w)}_{\sigma}\Biggl(\,\prod_{uv\in E(G\setminus w)}H(\tau_{u},\tau_{v})\Biggr)\Biggl(\,\prod_{v\in V(G\setminus w)}\mu^{(v,\sigma)}_{\tau_{v}}\Biggr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">because</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{(v,\sigma)}_{\tau_{v}}=\begin{cases}\lambda^{(v)}_{\tau_{v}},&amp;v\notin N(w),\\
H(\sigma,\tau_{v})\lambda^{(v)}_{\tau_{v}},&amp;v\in N(w),\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{(v,\sigma)}_{\tau_{v}}=\begin{cases}\lambda^{(v)}_{\tau_{v}},&amp;v\notin N(w),\\
H(\sigma,\tau_{v})\lambda^{(v)}_{\tau_{v}},&amp;v\in N(w),\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">and the second case is exactly</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot{\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})_{\tau_{v}}=H(\sigma,\tau_{v})\lambda^{(v)}_{\tau_{v}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot{\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})_{\tau_{v}}=H(\sigma,\tau_{v})\lambda^{(v)}_{\tau_{v}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, summing first over <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\tau}}\colon V(G\setminus w)\to I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝉</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\tau}}\colon V(G\setminus w)\to I</annotation></semantics></math> and then over <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in I</annotation></semantics></math> gives the desired recurrence.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in V(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in V(G)</annotation></semantics></math> be a vertex of maximum degree <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying the induction hypothesis to each summand in (<a href="#S5.E1" title="Equation 5.1 ‣ Lemma 5.1. ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>) reduces the induction step to proving</p>
<table id="S5.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{\sigma\in I}\lambda^{(w)}_{\sigma}\prod_{v\in V(G\setminus w)}Z_{f_{v}+1}({\bm{\mu}}^{(v,\sigma)})^{1/(f_{v}+1)}\geq\prod_{v\in V(G)}Z_{d_{v}+1}({\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})^{1/(d_{v}+1)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{\sigma\in I}\lambda^{(w)}_{\sigma}\prod_{v\in V(G\setminus w)}Z_{f_{v}+1}({\bm{\mu}}^{(v,\sigma)})^{1/(f_{v}+1)}\geq\prod_{v\in V(G)}Z_{d_{v}+1}({\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})^{1/(d_{v}+1)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where for <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V(G\setminus w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V(G\setminus w)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is the degree of vertex <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\setminus w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\setminus w</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V(G\setminus w)\setminus N(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V(G\setminus w)\setminus N(w)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{v}=d_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{v}=d_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\mu}}^{(v,\sigma)}={\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\mu}}^{(v,\sigma)}={\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the corresponding factors on both sides cancel. If <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in N(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in N(w)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{v}=d_{v}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{v}=d_{v}-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, (<a href="#S5.E2" title="Equation 5.2 ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>) reduces to</p>
<table id="S5.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\sigma\in I}\lambda^{(w)}_{\sigma}\prod_{v\in N(w)}Z_{d_{v}}({\bm{\mu}}^{(v,\sigma)})^{1/d_{v}}\geq\prod_{v\in\{w\}\cup N(w)}Z_{d_{v}+1}({\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})^{1/(d_{v}+1)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\sigma\in I}\lambda^{(w)}_{\sigma}\prod_{v\in N(w)}Z_{d_{v}}({\bm{\mu}}^{(v,\sigma)})^{1/d_{v}}\geq\prod_{v\in\{w\}\cup N(w)}Z_{d_{v}+1}({\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})^{1/(d_{v}+1)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{d}({\bm{\lambda}})\coloneqq Z_{d}({\bm{\lambda}})^{1/d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{d}({\bm{\lambda}})\coloneqq Z_{d}({\bm{\lambda}})^{1/d}</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition, <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\mu}}^{(v,\sigma)}=\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot{\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\mu}}^{(v,\sigma)}=\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot{\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in N(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in N(w)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{w}=\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{w}=\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, so the preceding inequality is equivalent to</p>
<table id="S5.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\sigma\in I}\lambda^{(w)}_{\sigma}\prod_{v\in N(w)}\frac{\Phi_{d_{v}}(\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot{\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})}{\Phi_{d_{v}+1}({\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})}\geq\Phi_{\Delta+1}({\bm{\lambda}}^{(w)})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\sigma\in I}\lambda^{(w)}_{\sigma}\prod_{v\in N(w)}\frac{\Phi_{d_{v}}(\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot{\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})}{\Phi_{d_{v}+1}({\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})}\geq\Phi_{\Delta+1}({\bm{\lambda}}^{(w)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p5.4" class="ltx_p">Indeed, this generalizes (<a href="#S1.E5" title="Equation 1.5 ‣ 1.4 Proof strategy ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.5</span></a>) mentioned in the introduction. Define the <em id="S5.SS1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">dual set</em></p>
<table id="S5.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}\coloneqq\{\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}:\forall\mathbf{z}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I},\,\mathbf{z}\cdot\mathbf{x}\geq\Phi_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z})\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}\coloneqq\{\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}:\forall\mathbf{z}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I},\,\mathbf{z}\cdot\mathbf{x}\geq\Phi_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z})\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p5.5" class="ltx_p">Then (<a href="#S5.E3" title="Equation 5.3 ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>) holds for every <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\lambda}}^{(w)}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\lambda}}^{(w)}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if</p>
<table id="S5.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Biggl(\,\prod_{v\in N(w)}\frac{\Phi_{d_{v}}(\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot{\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})}{\Phi_{d_{v}+1}({\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})}:\sigma\in I\Biggr)\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Biggl(\,\prod_{v\in N(w)}\frac{\Phi_{d_{v}}(\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot{\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})}{\Phi_{d_{v}+1}({\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})}:\sigma\in I\Biggr)\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p5.6" class="ltx_p">Observe that the vector in (<a href="#S5.E4" title="Equation 5.4 ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>) can be interpreted as a coordinatewise product of <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert N(w)\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert N(w)\rvert</annotation></semantics></math> vectors, one for each neighbor of <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, if <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> is closed under coordinatewise geometric mean, then we can reduce (<a href="#S5.E4" title="Equation 5.4 ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>) to a separate membership statement for each neighbor of <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>.
The next lemma establishes the required log-convexity.
The proof is essentially identical to that of Lemma 3.4 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite> and uses no structural information about <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, but only the fact that <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\Delta+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\Delta+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is a polynomial with nonnegative coefficients.
For <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m25" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log\mathbf{x}\coloneqq(\log x_{\sigma}:\sigma\in I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\mathbf{x}\coloneqq(\log x_{\sigma}:\sigma\in I)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.2</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}\coloneqq\{\log\mathbf{x}:\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}\coloneqq\{\log\mathbf{x}:\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is convex.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">The set <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> is relatively closed in <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the coordinatewise logarithm is a homeomorphism from <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{I}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> is closed, so it suffices to prove midpoint convexity. Fix <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and set <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{u}\coloneqq((x_{\sigma}y_{\sigma})^{1/2}:\sigma\in I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}\coloneqq((x_{\sigma}y_{\sigma})^{1/2}:\sigma\in I)</annotation></semantics></math>. We show <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, which amounts to showing that <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}\cdot\mathbf{u}\geq\Phi_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}\cdot\mathbf{u}\geq\Phi_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z})</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{1}\coloneqq((y_{\sigma}/x_{\sigma})^{1/2}z_{\sigma}:\sigma\in I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{1}\coloneqq((y_{\sigma}/x_{\sigma})^{1/2}z_{\sigma}:\sigma\in I)</annotation></semantics></math>, the assumption <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}\cdot\mathbf{u}=\mathbf{z}_{1}\cdot\mathbf{x}\geq\Phi_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z}_{1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}\cdot\mathbf{u}=\mathbf{z}_{1}\cdot\mathbf{x}\geq\Phi_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z}_{1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, for <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{2}\coloneqq((x_{\sigma}/y_{\sigma})^{1/2}z_{\sigma}:\sigma\in I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{2}\coloneqq((x_{\sigma}/y_{\sigma})^{1/2}z_{\sigma}:\sigma\in I)</annotation></semantics></math>, the assumption <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}\cdot\mathbf{u}=\mathbf{z}_{2}\cdot\mathbf{y}\geq\Phi_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z}_{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}\cdot\mathbf{u}=\mathbf{z}_{2}\cdot\mathbf{y}\geq\Phi_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z}_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the geometric mean of these inequalities shows that it suffices to prove <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z}_{1})\Phi_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z}_{2})\geq\Phi_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z}_{1})\Phi_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z}_{2})\geq\Phi_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is equivalent to</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z}_{1})Z_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z}_{2})\geq Z_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z})^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z}_{1})Z_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z}_{2})\geq Z_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z})^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">Write <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z})=\sum_{{\bm{\alpha}}}c_{{\bm{\alpha}}}\mathbf{z}^{{\bm{\alpha}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>𝜶</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝜶</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝜶</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z})=\sum_{{\bm{\alpha}}}c_{{\bm{\alpha}}}\mathbf{z}^{{\bm{\alpha}}}</annotation></semantics></math> in its monomial expansion. Since <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{{\bm{\alpha}}}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝜶</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{{\bm{\alpha}}}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜶</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the Cauchy–Schwarz inequality gives</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z}_{1})Z_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z}_{2})=\biggl(\sum_{{\bm{\alpha}}}c_{{\bm{\alpha}}}(\mathbf{z}_{1})^{{\bm{\alpha}}}\biggr)\biggl(\sum_{{\bm{\alpha}}}c_{{\bm{\alpha}}}(\mathbf{z}_{2})^{{\bm{\alpha}}}\biggr)\geq\biggl(\sum_{{\bm{\alpha}}}c_{{\bm{\alpha}}}((\mathbf{z}_{1})^{{\bm{\alpha}}}(\mathbf{z}_{2})^{{\bm{\alpha}}})^{1/2}\biggr)^{\!2}=Z_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z})^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>𝜶</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝜶</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝜶</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>𝜶</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝜶</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝜶</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>𝜶</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝜶</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝜶</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝜶</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z}_{1})Z_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z}_{2})=\biggl(\sum_{{\bm{\alpha}}}c_{{\bm{\alpha}}}(\mathbf{z}_{1})^{{\bm{\alpha}}}\biggr)\biggl(\sum_{{\bm{\alpha}}}c_{{\bm{\alpha}}}(\mathbf{z}_{2})^{{\bm{\alpha}}}\biggr)\geq\biggl(\sum_{{\bm{\alpha}}}c_{{\bm{\alpha}}}((\mathbf{z}_{1})^{{\bm{\alpha}}}(\mathbf{z}_{2})^{{\bm{\alpha}}})^{1/2}\biggr)^{\!2}=Z_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z})^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">where the last equality uses <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{z}_{1})_{\sigma}(\mathbf{z}_{2})_{\sigma}=z_{\sigma}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{z}_{1})_{\sigma}(\mathbf{z}_{2})_{\sigma}=z_{\sigma}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in I</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{z}_{1})^{{\bm{\alpha}}}(\mathbf{z}_{2})^{{\bm{\alpha}}}=(\mathbf{z}^{{\bm{\alpha}}})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝜶</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝜶</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝜶</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{z}_{1})^{{\bm{\alpha}}}(\mathbf{z}_{2})^{{\bm{\alpha}}}=(\mathbf{z}^{{\bm{\alpha}}})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S5.SS1.p6.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\alpha}}\in(\mathbb{N}_{0})^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\alpha}}\in(\mathbb{N}_{0})^{I}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">By <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 5.2. ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>, <a href="#S5.E4" title="In 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a> follows from the following.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.3</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq d\leq\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq d\leq\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\lambda}}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝛌</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\lambda}}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\biggl(\biggl(\frac{\Phi_{d}(\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot{\bm{\lambda}})}{\Phi_{d+1}({\bm{\lambda}})}\biggr)^{\!\Delta}:\sigma\in I\biggr)\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝝀</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.278em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\biggl(\biggl(\frac{\Phi_{d}(\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot{\bm{\lambda}})}{\Phi_{d+1}({\bm{\lambda}})}\biggr)^{\!\Delta}:\sigma\in I\biggr)\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Indeed, assume that <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 5.3. ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a> holds. Then, for each <math id="S5.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in N(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in N(w)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S5.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{v}\coloneqq\biggl(\biggl(\frac{\Phi_{d_{v}}(\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot{\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})}{\Phi_{d_{v}+1}({\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})}\biggr)^{\!\Delta}:\sigma\in I\biggr)\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.278em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{v}\coloneqq\biggl(\biggl(\frac{\Phi_{d_{v}}(\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot{\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})}{\Phi_{d_{v}+1}({\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})}\biggr)^{\!\Delta}:\sigma\in I\biggr)\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">This is the subproblem associated with <math id="S5.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> described immediately before <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 5.2. ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>.
Since <math id="S5.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert N(w)\rvert=\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert N(w)\rvert=\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 5.2. ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a> implies</p>
<table id="S5.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log\Biggl(\,\prod_{v\in N(w)}\frac{\Phi_{d_{v}}(\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot{\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})}{\Phi_{d_{v}+1}({\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})}:\sigma\in I\Biggr)=\sum_{v\in N(w)}\frac{1}{\Delta}\log\mathbf{x}_{v}\in\log\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mfrac><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\Biggl(\,\prod_{v\in N(w)}\frac{\Phi_{d_{v}}(\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot{\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})}{\Phi_{d_{v}+1}({\bm{\lambda}}^{(v)})}:\sigma\in I\Biggr)=\sum_{v\in N(w)}\frac{1}{\Delta}\log\mathbf{x}_{v}\in\log\mathcal{S}_{\Delta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p8.3" class="ltx_p">which is equivalent to (<a href="#S5.E4" title="Equation 5.4 ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>). Therefore, it remains to prove <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 5.3. ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Resolution of the local membership problem</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=K_{3}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>∘</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=K_{3}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>, the statement which corresponds to <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 5.3. ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a> appears as <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, Lemma 3.3]</cite>.
The case <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=d</annotation></semantics></math> of that statement is the tangent-plane inequality for the normalized clique partition function of clique size <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d+1</annotation></semantics></math>, while the case <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta&gt;d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta&gt;d</annotation></semantics></math> was proved by model-specific calculations and an iteration through consecutive degrees.
The same tangent-plane argument gives the starting point here.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s},\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s},\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="S5.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{x})\coloneqq\sum_{\sigma\in I}s_{\sigma}^{m-1}x_{\sigma},\quad\text{and}\quad M_{m}(\mathbf{s})\coloneqq\sup_{\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}}\frac{Z_{m}(\mathbf{x})}{D_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{x})^{m}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{x})\coloneqq\sum_{\sigma\in I}s_{\sigma}^{m-1}x_{\sigma},\quad\text{and}\quad M_{m}(\mathbf{s})\coloneqq\sup_{\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}}\frac{Z_{m}(\mathbf{x})}{D_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{x})^{m}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">By definition, <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{s})\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{s})\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if for all <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S5.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z})\leq D_{\Delta+1,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{z})=\sum_{\sigma\in I}s_{\sigma}^{\Delta}z_{\sigma}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{z})\leq D_{\Delta+1,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{z})=\sum_{\sigma\in I}s_{\sigma}^{\Delta}z_{\sigma}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Equivalently, <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(s_{\sigma}^{\Delta}:\sigma\in I)\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{\sigma}^{\Delta}:\sigma\in I)\in\mathcal{S}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let</p>
<table id="S5.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{d,\sigma}(\mathbf{x})\coloneqq\frac{\Phi_{d}(\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot\mathbf{x})}{\Phi_{d+1}(\mathbf{x})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{d,\sigma}(\mathbf{x})\coloneqq\frac{\Phi_{d}(\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot\mathbf{x})}{\Phi_{d+1}(\mathbf{x})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Thus, to prove <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 5.3. ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>, it suffices to show the following:</p>
<table id="S5.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{for all }\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I},\text{ if }\mathbf{s}\coloneqq(A_{d,\sigma}(\mathbf{x}):\sigma\in I),\text{ then }M_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{s})\leq 1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mtext> if </mtext><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mtext> then </mtext><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{for all }\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I},\text{ if }\mathbf{s}\coloneqq(A_{d,\sigma}(\mathbf{x}):\sigma\in I),\text{ then }M_{\Delta+1}(\mathbf{s})\leq 1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Let us denote this property by <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P}(d,\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P}(d,\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math>, corresponding to neighbor degree <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and clique size <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta+1</annotation></semantics></math>.
The next lemma verifies <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P}(m,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P}(m,m)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the promised starting point derived from the tangent-plane argument.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.4</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{s}\coloneqq(A_{m,\sigma}(\mathbf{x}):\sigma\in I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}\coloneqq(A_{m,\sigma}(\mathbf{x}):\sigma\in I)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{m+1}(\mathbf{s})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{m+1}(\mathbf{s})=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in I</annotation></semantics></math>, (<a href="#S2.E1" title="Equation 2.1 ‣ Lemma 2.6. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{\sigma}\Phi_{m+1}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>σ</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{\sigma}\Phi_{m+1}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{m+1}Z_{m+1}(\mathbf{x})^{-m/(m+1)}\cdot\partial_{\sigma}Z_{m+1}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>σ</mi></msub><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{m+1}Z_{m+1}(\mathbf{x})^{-m/(m+1)}\cdot\partial_{\sigma}Z_{m+1}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{m+1}Z_{m+1}(\mathbf{x})^{-m/(m+1)}\cdot(m+1)Z_{m}(\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{m+1}Z_{m+1}(\mathbf{x})^{-m/(m+1)}\cdot(m+1)Z_{m}(\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\biggl(\frac{\Phi_{m}(\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot\mathbf{x})}{\Phi_{m+1}(\mathbf{x})}\biggr)^{\!m}=s_{\sigma}^{m}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>σ</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\biggl(\frac{\Phi_{m}(\mathbf{m}_{\sigma}\odot\mathbf{x})}{\Phi_{m+1}(\mathbf{x})}\biggr)^{\!m}=s_{\sigma}^{m}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">By <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma 2.7. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.7</span></a>, <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{m+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{m+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is concave on the positive orthant, so for all <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{m+1}(\mathbf{z})\leq\Phi_{m+1}(\mathbf{x})+\sum_{\sigma\in I}\partial_{\sigma}\Phi_{m+1}(\mathbf{x})(z_{\sigma}-x_{\sigma})=\sum_{\sigma\in I}\partial_{\sigma}\Phi_{m+1}(\mathbf{x})z_{\sigma}=\sum_{\sigma\in I}s_{\sigma}^{m}z_{\sigma}=D_{m+1,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{z})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>σ</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>σ</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>σ</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{m+1}(\mathbf{z})\leq\Phi_{m+1}(\mathbf{x})+\sum_{\sigma\in I}\partial_{\sigma}\Phi_{m+1}(\mathbf{x})(z_{\sigma}-x_{\sigma})=\sum_{\sigma\in I}\partial_{\sigma}\Phi_{m+1}(\mathbf{x})z_{\sigma}=\sum_{\sigma\in I}s_{\sigma}^{m}z_{\sigma}=D_{m+1,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{z}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Here, the first equality uses <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\sigma\in I}\partial_{\sigma}\Phi_{m+1}(\mathbf{x})x_{\sigma}=\Phi_{m+1}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∂</mo><mi>σ</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\sigma\in I}\partial_{\sigma}\Phi_{m+1}(\mathbf{x})x_{\sigma}=\Phi_{m+1}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>, which follows from <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 2.1 (Euler’s homogeneous function theorem). ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>, since <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{m+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{m+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is homogeneous of degree 1. Therefore, <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{m+1}(\mathbf{s})\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{m+1}(\mathbf{s})\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}=\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}=\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> gives equality in (<a href="#S5.E5" title="Equation 5.5 ‣ Proof. ‣ 5.2 Resolution of the local membership problem ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.5</span></a>), so <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{m+1}(\mathbf{s})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{m+1}(\mathbf{s})=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">It remains to prove that <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P}(d,d^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P}(d,d^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P}(d,d^{\prime}+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P}(d,d^{\prime}+1)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq d\leq d^{\prime}&lt;\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq d\leq d^{\prime}&lt;\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
The key idea is to realize <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log M_{m}(\mathbf{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log M_{m}(\mathbf{s})</annotation></semantics></math> as the optimized pressure <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{m}(\mathbf{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{m}(\mathbf{s})</annotation></semantics></math> of the abstract system introduced in <a href="#S4" title="4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, thereby allowing us to apply <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>.
The resulting monotonicity property of <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{m}(\mathbf{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{m}(\mathbf{s})</annotation></semantics></math> proves the desired implication from <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P}(d,d^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P}(d,d^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P}(d,d^{\prime}+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P}(d,d^{\prime}+1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the abstract setting of <a href="#S4" title="4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, let the set of letters be <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\coloneqq I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>≔</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\coloneqq I</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{m}\coloneqq I^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><msup><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{m}\coloneqq I^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, and define the energy function by</p>
<table id="S5.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U_{m,\mathbf{s}}({\bm{\omega}})\coloneqq\sum_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq m}\log H(\omega_{i},\omega_{j})-(m-1)\sum_{j=1}^{m}\log s_{\omega_{j}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U_{m,\mathbf{s}}({\bm{\omega}})\coloneqq\sum_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq m}\log H(\omega_{i},\omega_{j})-(m-1)\sum_{j=1}^{m}\log s_{\omega_{j}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">which is well-defined because <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}</annotation></semantics></math> are entrywise positive. Clearly, each <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is nonempty, <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\Omega_{m}:m\geq 1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Omega_{m}:m\geq 1)</annotation></semantics></math> is permutation-invariant and deletion-compatible, and <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{m,\mathbf{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{m,\mathbf{s}}</annotation></semantics></math> is permutation-invariant. The corresponding partition function and the optimized pressure are denoted by</p>
<table id="S5.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{Z}_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\alpha)\coloneqq\sum_{{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}}\exp(U_{m,\mathbf{s}}({\bm{\omega}}))\prod_{j=1}^{m}\alpha(\omega_{j})\quad\text{and}\quad F_{m}(\mathbf{s})\coloneqq\sup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)}\log\mathcal{Z}_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\alpha)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{Z}_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\alpha)\coloneqq\sum_{{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}}\exp(U_{m,\mathbf{s}}({\bm{\omega}}))\prod_{j=1}^{m}\alpha(\omega_{j})\quad\text{and}\quad F_{m}(\mathbf{s})\coloneqq\sup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)}\log\mathcal{Z}_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\alpha),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p">respectively.
The pair-interaction terms in <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{m,\mathbf{s}}({\bm{\omega}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{m,\mathbf{s}}({\bm{\omega}})</annotation></semantics></math>, which form the first sum in the definition, reproduce the weight of a spin assignment on <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}</annotation></semantics></math>-dependent terms introduce the normalization factors <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\sigma}^{-(m-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\sigma}^{-(m-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, chosen so that</p>
<table id="S5.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\alpha)=Z_{m}(\alpha(\sigma)s_{\sigma}^{-(m-1)}:\sigma\in I)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\alpha)=Z_{m}(\alpha(\sigma)s_{\sigma}^{-(m-1)}:\sigma\in I),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.4" class="ltx_p">thereby allowing us to compare <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{m}(\mathbf{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{m}(\mathbf{s})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{m}(\mathbf{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{m}(\mathbf{s})</annotation></semantics></math>.
This comparison is given in <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5.5. ‣ 5.2 Resolution of the local membership problem ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.5</span></a>.
The coefficient <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m-1</annotation></semantics></math> will also ensure that the family of energies satisfies the deletion identity <a href="#S4.Ex5" title="Item (2) ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(2)</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.5</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{m}(\mathbf{s})=\log M_{m}(\mathbf{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{m}(\mathbf{s})=\log M_{m}(\mathbf{s})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, define <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathbf{x}}\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathbf{x}}\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathbf{x}}(\sigma)\coloneqq\frac{s_{\sigma}^{m-1}x_{\sigma}}{D_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{x})},\qquad\sigma\in I." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathbf{x}}(\sigma)\coloneqq\frac{s_{\sigma}^{m-1}x_{\sigma}}{D_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{x})},\qquad\sigma\in I.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">The map <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\mapsto\alpha_{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\mapsto\alpha_{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a bijection from <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}:D_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{x})=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}:D_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{x})=1\}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)</annotation></semantics></math> with the inverse <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha\mapsto(\alpha(\sigma)s_{\sigma}^{-(m-1)}:\sigma\in I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\mapsto(\alpha(\sigma)s_{\sigma}^{-(m-1)}:\sigma\in I)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Suppose <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{x})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{x})=1</annotation></semantics></math> and set <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\alpha_{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\alpha_{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then by definition,</span></p>
<table id="S5.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\alpha)=Z_{m}(\alpha(\sigma)s_{\sigma}^{-(m-1)}:\sigma\in I)=Z_{m}(\mathbf{x})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\alpha)=Z_{m}(\alpha(\sigma)s_{\sigma}^{-(m-1)}:\sigma\in I)=Z_{m}(\mathbf{x}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">To elaborate, summing</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(U_{m,\mathbf{s}}({\bm{\omega}}))\prod_{j=1}^{m}\alpha(\omega_{j})=\prod_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq m}H(\omega_{i},\omega_{j})\prod_{j=1}^{m}(\alpha(\omega_{j})s_{\omega_{j}}^{-(m-1)})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(U_{m,\mathbf{s}}({\bm{\omega}}))\prod_{j=1}^{m}\alpha(\omega_{j})=\prod_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq m}H(\omega_{i},\omega_{j})\prod_{j=1}^{m}(\alpha(\omega_{j})s_{\omega_{j}}^{-(m-1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">over <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\bm{\omega}}=(\omega_{j}:j\in[m])\in I^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\omega}}=(\omega_{j}:j\in[m])\in I^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> proves (<a href="#S5.E8" title="Equation 5.8 ‣ Proof. ‣ 5.2 Resolution of the local membership problem ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.8</span></a>).
Using (<a href="#S5.E8" title="Equation 5.8 ‣ Proof. ‣ 5.2 Resolution of the local membership problem ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.8</span></a>) together with the bijection <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\mapsto\alpha_{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\mapsto\alpha_{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="F_{m}(\mathbf{s})=\sup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)}\log\mathcal{Z}_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\alpha)=\sup_{\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}:D_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{x})=1}\log Z_{m}(\mathbf{x})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>log</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{m}(\mathbf{s})=\sup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)}\log\mathcal{Z}_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\alpha)=\sup_{\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}:D_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{x})=1}\log Z_{m}(\mathbf{x}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">Since both <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{m}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{m}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{x})^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{x})^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> are homogeneous of degree <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sup_{\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}:D_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{x})=1}\log Z_{m}(\mathbf{x})=\sup_{\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}}\log\biggl(\frac{Z_{m}(\mathbf{x})}{D_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{x})^{m}}\biggr)=\log M_{m}(\mathbf{s})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}:D_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{x})=1}\log Z_{m}(\mathbf{x})=\sup_{\mathbf{x}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}}\log\biggl(\frac{Z_{m}(\mathbf{x})}{D_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\mathbf{x})^{m}}\biggr)=\log M_{m}(\mathbf{s}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p6.6.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{m}(\mathbf{s})=\log M_{m}(\mathbf{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{m}(\mathbf{s})=\log M_{m}(\mathbf{s})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we show that the current setting satisfies the required properties, thereby allowing us to apply <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.6</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every fixed <math id="S5.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, the partition function <math id="S5.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S5.E7" title="Equation 5.7 ‣ 5.2 Resolution of the local membership problem ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.7</span></a>) and the energy function in (<a href="#S5.E6" title="Equation 5.6 ‣ 5.2 Resolution of the local membership problem ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.6</span></a>) satisfy <a href="#S4.I1.i1" title="Item (1) ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(1)</span></a> and <a href="#S4.Ex5" title="Item (2) ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(2)</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first verify <a href="#S4.I1.i1" title="Item (1) ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(1)</span></a>. Fix <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{P}^{+}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall that <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{m}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{m}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined by</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{m}^{\alpha}({\bm{\omega}})\coloneqq\frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\alpha)}\exp(U_{m,\mathbf{s}}({\bm{\omega}}))\prod_{j=1}^{m}\alpha(\omega_{j})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{m}^{\alpha}({\bm{\omega}})\coloneqq\frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\alpha)}\exp(U_{m,\mathbf{s}}({\bm{\omega}}))\prod_{j=1}^{m}\alpha(\omega_{j}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">is an exchangeable law on <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. For simplicity, write <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\coloneqq\mu_{m}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>≔</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\coloneqq\mu_{m}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. We claim that the count-generating polynomial of <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="S5.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h_{\mu}(\mathbf{z})=\frac{Z_{m}(\alpha(\sigma)s_{\sigma}^{-(m-1)}z_{\sigma}:\sigma\in I)}{\mathcal{Z}_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\alpha)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>σ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mu}(\mathbf{z})=\frac{Z_{m}(\alpha(\sigma)s_{\sigma}^{-(m-1)}z_{\sigma}:\sigma\in I)}{\mathcal{Z}_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\alpha)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Indeed, by definition,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mu}(\mathbf{z})=\sum_{{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}}\mu({\bm{\omega}})\mathbf{z}^{T({\bm{\omega}})},\qquad\mathbf{z}^{T({\bm{\omega}})}=\prod_{j=1}^{m}z_{\omega_{j}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mu}(\mathbf{z})=\sum_{{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}}\mu({\bm{\omega}})\mathbf{z}^{T({\bm{\omega}})},\qquad\mathbf{z}^{T({\bm{\omega}})}=\prod_{j=1}^{m}z_{\omega_{j}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">For each <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\alpha)\mu({\bm{\omega}})\mathbf{z}^{T({\bm{\omega}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{m,\mathbf{s}}(\alpha)\mu({\bm{\omega}})\mathbf{z}^{T({\bm{\omega}})}</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(U_{m,\mathbf{s}}({\bm{\omega}}))\prod_{j=1}^{m}(\alpha(\omega_{j})z_{\omega_{j}})=\prod_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq m}H(\omega_{i},\omega_{j})\prod_{j=1}^{m}(\alpha(\omega_{j})z_{\omega_{j}}s_{\omega_{j}}^{-(m-1)})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(U_{m,\mathbf{s}}({\bm{\omega}}))\prod_{j=1}^{m}(\alpha(\omega_{j})z_{\omega_{j}})=\prod_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq m}H(\omega_{i},\omega_{j})\prod_{j=1}^{m}(\alpha(\omega_{j})z_{\omega_{j}}s_{\omega_{j}}^{-(m-1)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">Summing over <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> gives exactly</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Z_{m}(\alpha(\sigma)s_{\sigma}^{-(m-1)}z_{\sigma}:\sigma\in I)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{m}(\alpha(\sigma)s_{\sigma}^{-(m-1)}z_{\sigma}:\sigma\in I),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p8.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p8.6.1" class="ltx_text">which proves (<a href="#S5.E9" title="Equation 5.9 ‣ Proof. ‣ 5.2 Resolution of the local membership problem ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.9</span></a>). By <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma 2.7. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.7</span></a>, <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lorentzian, and <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem5" title="Proposition 2.5. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a> shows that <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> is also Lorentzian. Therefore, <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{N}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{N}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we verify <a href="#S4.Ex5" title="Item (2) ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(2)</span></a>. Fix <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\omega}}\in\Omega_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. The energy <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{m,\mathbf{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{m,\mathbf{s}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sum of pair-interaction terms and linear terms. Pair-interaction terms satisfy</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{m}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}1\leq i&lt;j\leq m\\
i,j\neq k\end{subarray}}\log H(\omega_{i},\omega_{j})=(m-2)\sum_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq m}\log H(\omega_{i},\omega_{j})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{m}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}1\leq i&lt;j\leq m\\
i,j\neq k\end{subarray}}\log H(\omega_{i},\omega_{j})=(m-2)\sum_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq m}\log H(\omega_{i},\omega_{j}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">because each pair <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> survives exactly <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m-2</annotation></semantics></math> of the <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> single-site deletions. Linear terms satisfy</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{m}\biggl(-(m-2)\sum_{i\in[m]\setminus\{k\}}\log s_{\omega_{i}}\biggr)=-(m-2)(m-1)\sum_{i=1}^{m}\log s_{\omega_{i}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{m}\biggl(-(m-2)\sum_{i\in[m]\setminus\{k\}}\log s_{\omega_{i}}\biggr)=-(m-2)(m-1)\sum_{i=1}^{m}\log s_{\omega_{i}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">because each site <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> survives exactly <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m-1</annotation></semantics></math> deletions. Combining these gives</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{m}U_{m-1,\mathbf{s}}({\bm{\omega}}_{[m]\setminus k})=(m-2)U_{m,\mathbf{s}}({\bm{\omega}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝎</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{m}U_{m-1,\mathbf{s}}({\bm{\omega}}_{[m]\setminus k})=(m-2)U_{m,\mathbf{s}}({\bm{\omega}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">which is exactly <a href="#S4.Ex5" title="Item (2) ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(2)</span></a> for the energy function <math id="S5.SS2.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{m,\mathbf{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{m,\mathbf{s}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S5.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma 5.6. ‣ 5.2 Resolution of the local membership problem ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemmas</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.6</span></a> and <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 4.2. ‣ 4 Optimized pressure and its monotonicity ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> imply that, for <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S5.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="mF_{m-1}(\mathbf{s})\geq(m-2)F_{m}(\mathbf{s})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">mF_{m-1}(\mathbf{s})\geq(m-2)F_{m}(\mathbf{s}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p10.2" class="ltx_p">Finally, we prove <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 5.3. ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 5.3. ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\lambda}}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\lambda}}\in(\mathbb{R}^{+})^{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{s}\coloneqq(A_{d,\sigma}({\bm{\lambda}}):\sigma\in I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}\coloneqq(A_{d,\sigma}({\bm{\lambda}}):\sigma\in I)</annotation></semantics></math>.
<a href="#S5.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 5.4. ‣ 5.2 Resolution of the local membership problem ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a> implies <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{d+1}(\mathbf{s})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{d+1}(\mathbf{s})=1</annotation></semantics></math>, which gives <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P}(d,d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P}(d,d)</annotation></semantics></math>.
This immediately gives <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P}(d,\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P}(d,\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=d</annotation></semantics></math>, so assume <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq d&lt;\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq d&lt;\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Suppose <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq d\leq d^{\prime}&lt;\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq d\leq d^{\prime}&lt;\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P}(d,d^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P}(d,d^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> holds.
By <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5.5. ‣ 5.2 Resolution of the local membership problem ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.5</span></a>, <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{d^{\prime}+1}(\mathbf{s})=\log M_{d^{\prime}+1}(\mathbf{s})\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{d^{\prime}+1}(\mathbf{s})=\log M_{d^{\prime}+1}(\mathbf{s})\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, so (<a href="#S5.E10" title="Equation 5.10 ‣ 5.2 Resolution of the local membership problem ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.10</span></a>) with <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=d^{\prime}+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=d^{\prime}+2</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{d^{\prime}+2}(\mathbf{s})\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{d^{\prime}+2}(\mathbf{s})\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, where we use the fact that the coefficient <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m-2=d^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m-2=d^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is nonzero.
Applying <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5.5. ‣ 5.2 Resolution of the local membership problem ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.5</span></a> again gives <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{d^{\prime}+2}(\mathbf{s})\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{d^{\prime}+2}(\mathbf{s})\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P}(d,d^{\prime}+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P}(d,d^{\prime}+1)</annotation></semantics></math> holds.
Therefore, <math id="S5.SS2.p11.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P}(d,\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P}(d,\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math> holds, which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p">By the reduction in <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 5.3. ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a> implies (<a href="#S5.E3" title="Equation 5.3 ‣ 5.1 Inductive localization and the dual set ‣ 5 Clique minimization for antiferromagnetic models ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>) and therefore completes the induction step. This proves <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 1.2. ‣ 1.1 A vertex-inhomogeneous strengthening ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Antiferromagnetic models are clique-minimizing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Concluding remarks</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A natural next problem is to determine the precise scope of the clique-minimizing phenomenon.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_problem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Problem 6.1</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Characterize all clique-minimizing models.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As mentioned in the introduction, the class of clique-minimizing models strictly contains the class of antiferromagnetic models. Let <math id="S6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be antiferromagnetic models on spin sets <math id="S6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, and let <math id="S6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\coloneqq H_{1}\otimes H_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\coloneqq H_{1}\otimes H_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\otimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\otimes</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the tensor product. That is, <math id="S6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> has the spin set <math id="S6.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{1}\times I_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{1}\times I_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="S6.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M((\sigma_{1},\sigma_{2}),(\tau_{1},\tau_{2}))\coloneqq H_{1}(\sigma_{1},\tau_{1})H_{2}(\sigma_{2},\tau_{2}),\qquad\sigma_{1},\tau_{1}\in I_{1},\ \sigma_{2},\tau_{2}\in I_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M((\sigma_{1},\sigma_{2}),(\tau_{1},\tau_{2}))\coloneqq H_{1}(\sigma_{1},\tau_{1})H_{2}(\sigma_{2},\tau_{2}),\qquad\sigma_{1},\tau_{1}\in I_{1},\ \sigma_{2},\tau_{2}\in I_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The eigenvalues of <math id="S6.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="S6.p2.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\eta_{i}\rho_{j}:i\in I_{1},\,j\in I_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\eta_{i}\rho_{j}:i\in I_{1},\,j\in I_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S6.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\eta_{i}:i\in I_{1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\eta_{i}:i\in I_{1}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\rho_{j}:j\in I_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\rho_{j}:j\in I_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math> are the multisets of eigenvalues of <math id="S6.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. Thus, if <math id="S6.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> have negative eigenvalues, then <math id="S6.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is not antiferromagnetic.
On the other hand, for every graph <math id="S6.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
